  `c_5_embedding`: [],
  `c_layer_path`: 'Idea/Bimba/World/Types/Coordinates/C/C1',
  `c_layer_role`: 'forms_templates',
  `crystallisation_state`: 'incubating_type_index',
  `q_0_unformed_source_condition`: 'C1 Form presupposes what it is the form OF. Before any reusable pattern can be authored, a canonical source-ground must already stand: C1 is Defined by C0 (CLAUDE.md II.E), so its thrown horizon is the Bimba/source-condition of which a Form is the essential-nature articulation. A Form authored about nothing forms nothing. Beneath C0 lies the deeper void-pole the matheme names: the scalar component a_b of the bimba-quaternion, \'quantitative-without-quality, the 0 of the 0/1, the magnitude-without-direction\' (kernel §1) — the unmarked openness from which the first explicit articulation has not yet differentiated. C1\'s pre-given condition is precisely that undifferentiated scalar void: Definition (#1) is the FIRST explicit mark that crystallises out of it, \'three directional components emerging from the scalar void as the first explicit triad.\' So C1 arises from a horizon it can never restate — the source must already be given (C0), and beneath that the void must already hold itself open, before Form has anything to make recognisable-again. The unstated that C1 presupposes is: there is a ground; there is something there to characterise; the lakṣaṇa has a bearer.',
  `q_1_form_as_essential_nature`: '',
