MATCH (n:Bimba {coordinate: 'C2'}) SET n += {
  `c_1_ct_type`: 'CT1',
  `c_3_moc_evidence_paths`: ['Idea/Bimba/World/Types/Coordinates/C/C2/C2.canvas', 'Idea/Bimba/World/Types/Coordinates/C/C2/C2.md'],
  `c_4_artifact_role`: 'type-moc-pointer',
  `c_4_layer`: 'COORDINATE',
  `c_5_crystallisation_state`: 'incubating_type_index',
  `c_layer_path`: 'Idea/Bimba/World/Types/Coordinates/C/C2',
  `c_layer_role`: 'entities_properties_tags',
  `crystallisation_state`: 'incubating_type_index',
  `q_0_instantiation_thrownness`: 'C2 Entity does not begin; it is begun. Its thrown ground is C1 Form: an entity cannot stand until there is already a definitional pattern for it to instantiate — \'C1 Instantiated through C2\' (CLAUDE.md II.E). Behind C1 stands C0 Bimba, the canonical source; so C2\'s horizon is the full descent #1 Definition arriving out of #0 Ground, the raw archetype #2 (Operation) emerging the instant a Form becomes available to be enacted. But the deeper, more honest void-pole is operational, not just genealogical: every entity here arises from an UNRESOLVED capture — the loose wikilink, the root-created note, the Empty-captured fragment that has a name but no settled home (C2.md, Hen Use). That pre-articulate residue is the \'that\' C2 presupposes: there is a mention, a pointing-toward, before there is a thing. The entity is the resolution of that thrownness — Hen\'s routing through C2 after Empty capture is precisely the act of giving a captured pointer its first articulation as a discrete, propertied unit. C2\'s ground is therefore double: the prior Form it instantiates, and the unresolved reference it answers. It is the position that owes its existence to two debts at once — to the definition above it and to the unkept pointer behind it.',
  `q_1_candidate_substance`: '',
  `q_1_entity_typology`: '',
