MATCH (n:Bimba {coordinate: 'C3'}) SET n += {
  `c_1_ct_type`: 'CT1',
  `c_3_moc_evidence_paths`: ['Idea/Bimba/World/Types/Coordinates/C/C3/C3.canvas', 'Idea/Bimba/World/Types/Coordinates/C/C3/C3.md'],
  `c_4_artifact_role`: 'type-moc-pointer',
  `c_4_layer`: 'COORDINATE',
  `c_5_crystallisation_state`: 'incubating_type_index',
  `c_layer_path`: 'Idea/Bimba/World/Types/Coordinates/C/C3',
  `c_layer_role`: 'processes_canvases_diagrams',
  `crystallisation_state`: 'incubating_type_index',
  `q_0_revealed_from_entity`: 'C3 Process has nothing to organise until something stands to be organised. Its thrown ground is C2 — the family\'s atomic entities — for in the C-family\'s own derivation chain the Entity \'reveals its processual nature as\' Process (CLAUDE.md II.E): process is not posited, it is disclosed out of already-related units. Beneath C2 lies the raw archetype #3 (Pattern) emerging from #2 (Operation): the canvas cannot pattern anything until operative atoms exist to be patterned, just as the matheme\'s pulse of Becoming presupposes the two poles it oscillates between. C3\'s void-pole is therefore double. First, it presupposes the prior population of the typology with definable Forms (C1) and atomic Entities (C2) whose couplings it will lay out. Second — and this is its proper darkness — it presupposes the not-yet: the live architecture diagram still under active spec development, the workflow not yet stable, the canvas in motion that \'remains Seed evidence until crystallised\' (C3.md). C3 stands on the unstabilised: every process-form it will hold was once an undeveloped diagram, and the horizon it arises from is precisely that field of process-in-formation that has not yet earned the name of a reusable type. The ground of Process is process-before-it-can-be-categorised.',
  `q_1_process_form_typology`: '',
  `q_2_canvas_in_motion`: '',
  `s_1_vault_path`: 'Idea/Bimba/World/Types/Coordinates/C/C3/C3.md',
