  `coordinate_prefix`: 'S2',
  `promotion_source`: 'pi_agent',
  `q_0_substrate_not_semantics`: '',
  `q_1_graph_body_definition`: '',
  `q_2_raw_graph_cache_operations`: '',
  `q_3_torus_shared_arena`: '',
  `q_4_purity_of_role`: 'S2 exists to be the SHARED FLOOR beneath graph meaning — so that every higher graph-, retrieval-, and memory-facing concern stands on one common relational arena and one common volatile arena rather than fragmenting into private stores. Its telos is purity of role: \'The return of S2 is therefore purity of role: one shared relational floor, one shared volatile floor, and no semantic inflation inside the substrate\' (S2.md). Its genealogy is the third manifestation within the S-family — #2 (raw archetype Operation/Entity) → S2 (GraphDB Substrate), the descent of Operation into the technology stack as raw Cypher, raw key-value, and connection/transaction primitives. Its locality in the S-SYSTEM-INDEX system image is exact: \'S2 makes it graph/vector/cache real,\' the layer whose primary data authority is graph nodes/edges, vector handles, and retrieval/cache records. Its discipline is anti-inflation: \'every higher graph-facing concern must stand on this floor, but none may collapse back into it\' (S2.md) — a node may bear coordinate meaning, but the meaning is S2\'s tenant, not S2\'s law. Read teleologically, S2 is why the whole system can have ONE graph rather than many: the schema-agnostic, namespace-capable substrate that lets canonical ontology, ingested corpus, and lived memory share a physical home without contaminating one another. Purpose: to be the common relational and volatile ground on which graph meaning is built but into which it is never folded.',
  `q_5_substrate_returns_pure`: 'S2 closes by RETURNING TO PURITY rather than accumulating meaning — its synthesis is a refusal to become what it hosts. Where most positions close by sedimenting their reflections back into ground, S2\'s 5→0 is inverse-disciplinary: every cycle of graph meaning that rides the substrate (Bimba topology, Gnostic retrieval, Graphiti episode) must, at S2\'s level, leave the substrate exactly as raw as it found it — \'no semantic inflation inside the substrate.\' The return is the re-affirmation of the substrate/semantics split: meaning routes up through S2\' and back, but S2 itself remains \'one shared relational floor, one shared volatile floor\' (S2.md). This is the matheme\'s 5→0 held as boundary-maintenance: S2 (the raw operational arena, the substrate-pole) and S2\' (the coordinate-aware semantic surface, its prime) are one layer read from two faces, joined by the twist that lets all meaning live in the prime while the base stays pure. And S2 OPENS rather than concludes because the substrate\'s destiny keeps enlarging: the universal graph \'remains the destiny of the layer\' (S2.md), and each cycle adds new namespaces, new corpus, new episodic memory to the shared physical base — the arena grows in capacity even as its semantic emptiness is conserved. The epogdoon η = log(9/8) keeps it one whole-tone short of closure (kernel-spec §0): the universal graph is never fully arrived, each cycle extends the shared floor without ever letting it become the meaning it bears. S2 is the substrate that is never finished being host — the common arena that re-opens, wider and still raw, every cycle.',
  `s_0_owned_by_coordinate`: 'M5-2',
  `s_1_vault_wikilink`: '[[S2]]',
  `s_2_crud_scope`: 'graph node/relation CRUD, schema, ingestion, retrieval',
  `s_2_query_discriminator`: 'coordinate',
  `s_2_query_prefix`: 'S',
  `s_4_function_role`: 'Direct S2 technical stack layer',
  `s_4_input_contracts`: '{"promotion_intent":"S2GraphPromotionIntent","property_proposals":"PropertyProposal evidence validated before node mutation","relationship_candidates":"registered typed relations with evidence"}',
  `s_4_output_contracts`: '{"neo4j":"coordinate-owned nodes and typed relationships","graphiti":"episode plans only; runtime remains S3 and invocation governance S5"}',
  `s_4_queryable_properties`: '{"identity":"coordinate","schema":"graph-schema registries","agent_surface":"epi graph promote-intent"}',
