MATCH (n:Bimba {coordinate: 'S3'}) SET n += {
  `artifact_kind`: 'vault_markdown',
  `c_0_core_nature`: 'Live session, gateway, transport, and runtime subscription boundary for active system state.',
  `c_1_description`: 'WebSocket gateway; session store; presence layer; shared execution substrate across processes and surfaces',
  `c_1_form`: 'Idea/Bimba/World/Types/Coordinates/S/S3/S3.md',
  `c_1_prior_description`: 'Live session, gateway, transport, and runtime subscription boundary for active system state.',
  `c_1_prior_name`: 'Gateway',
  `c_1_structure`: '{"authority_spec":"docs/specs/S/S3-S3i-GATEWAY.md","layer_name":"gateway-control-plane","promotion_contract":"s-branch-live-promotion-v1"}',
  `c_4_artifact_role`: 'definition',
  `content_hash`: 'sha256:4154c64ad7f3d89a88af9ec6f5fcc79c80e9d9984fdd02af344db00b3ebd5c48',
  `coordinate_axis`: 'direct',
  `coordinate_depth`: 1,
  `coordinate_family`: 'S',
  `coordinate_kind`: 'root_direct',
  `coordinate_namespace`: 'S',
  `coordinate_parent`: 'S',
  `coordinate_prefix`: 'S3',
  `promotion_source`: 'pi_agent',
  `q_0_field_before_command`: 'Before S3 can govern command it presupposes a substrate to carry it and a runtime to inhabit — S0\'s socket/process ground beneath the listener, S2\'s Neo4j/Redis beneath session and presence state (S3 \'also hosts spacetime + redis-context at S3\'\', CLAUDE.md II.C). As the S-family\'s manifestation of the raw #3 archetype (Pattern/Process, CLAUDE.md II.A), S3\'s void-pole is the un-routed field: a connection not yet handshaken, a request not yet validated, a session not yet bound to identity — the bare socket that has opened but to which no governed response, no lineage, no authority has yet been assigned. This is the thrown ground S3 stands upon: that there is transport at all, a wire that can carry frames, prior to any law about which session a frame belongs to or what subagent may inherit from what parent. \'A session is not first real because it is displayed somewhere; it is first real because S3 has accepted and governed it\' (S3.md) — so S3\'s q_0 is exactly the moment before that acceptance: the ungoverned invocation, the raw addressability that precedes sovereignty. The horizon S3 lives upon is command-as-possibility: an open command plane that can route, persist, and emit anything precisely because it has not yet routed this. Before session authority, the bare connection that consents to be governed; before the imperative plane acts, it is merely reachable.',
  `q_1_gateway_control_plane`: 'S3 IS the Gateway Control Plane — \'the imperative plane of the stack … the layer where command becomes lawfully actionable: the place where a participant, operator, or client addresses the system and expects a governed response. Its task is not merely transport. Its task is sovereignty at the level of invocation\' (S3.md). Against the other S-layers it is the one that \'makes it temporal and routed\' (S-SYSTEM-INDEX) — where S0 grounds, S1 resides, S2 stores, S3 GOVERNS COMMAND. Its substance is the stable WebSocket/RPC command surface with Epi-Claw Parity as \'a hard compatibility requirement rather than a vague aspiration\' (S3.md): the runtime in Body/S/S3/{gateway, gateway-contract} that \'accepts socket connections, emits a hello-ok frame, negotiates protocol/features, requires a connect handshake, validates method payloads, executes gateway-owned mutations, emits ordered events, and returns structured responses or structured errors.\' It is also \'the authority layer for Session identity\' — binding a session to canonical key, aliases, day identity, NOW path, workspace root, bootstrap scope, and subagent lineage (S3.md). The strict boundary defines it: \'imperative command belongs to S3; shared synchronized world-state belongs to S3\'\' — S3 \'validates, routes, persists, emits, and governs, but does not pretend to be the whole world. It is the control plane, not the inhabitable field.\' Definitionally S3 is the manifestation of #3 Process in the technology stack: the sovereign command-and-session plane where invocation becomes governed action. (PAI/plugin/harness readings \'remain part of the genealogy … but they are no longer the target shape\' — S3.md.)',
  `q_2_routes_governs_emits`: 'S3 moves by GOVERNING and EMITTING — its native act is the connection-and-authority lifecycle: it \'validates, routes, persists, emits, and governs\' (S3.md). The operations are concrete (S3.md p2): connection and authentication lifecycle; gateway-owned command, chat, session, config, channel, node, and approval surfaces; session identity, workspace, bootstrap, and subagent lineage law. Its method manifest is a real families\' grouping — connection/transport, agent runtime, chat runtime, session authority, config/system control, skills/models, channels/temporal control, node/device/browser/approval — and its event fanout is \'concrete rather than symbolic: agent, chat, tick, health, and heartbeat are named event families with sequence semantics and reconnect implications\' (S3.md). S3 couples in two directions and is actualised by four ta-onta carriers (S3.md): Chronos gives command \'a lawful cadence, schedule, and recurrence surface\'; Khora binds \'session authority to root, day, and NOW inheritance\'; Hen ensures gateway-bound identity \'corresponds to real vault structures\'; Anima turns gateway authority \'into dispatchable multi-agent action\'; Aletheia carries \'the consequences of command toward the shared-state plane of S3\'.\' The relational signature is governance-of-lineage: S3 \'decides which session a run belongs to, what subagent may inherit or spawn from what parent, what workspace and bootstrap scope apply\' — the authority that makes invocation belong to someone. It does not inhabit the world; it routes the command that acts on it, then hands consequence up to S3\' for rendering as shared state.',
  `q_3_torus_two_plane_architecture`: 'S3\'s organising structure is the TORUS — the live node carries this topology, and it is its home register and deepest structural truth: the gateway is a self-enclosing request/response/event loop. Structurally S3 is governed by the Two-Plane Architecture (S3.md p3): \'imperative command belongs to S3; shared synchronized world-state belongs to S3\'.\' This is the constitutive seam — S3 owns \'command execution first: run registration, transcript writes, session mutation, terminal snapshot caching, event emission, and operator-facing truth about the runtime,\' while S3\' \'only takes over once those imperative consequences must be rendered as shared state.\' The loop closes: a connection opens (hello-ok), handshakes (connect), issues governed methods, receives ordered events with sequence/reconnect semantics, and its consequences fold up into the shared field — the torus of governed invocation. The structural laws that hold it non-degenerate are the parity and authority contracts: Epi-Claw Parity means \'behavioral equivalence of the command plane\' (an epi-claw-shaped client receives \'the same category of capability with truthful semantics\'), and \'no fake completeness: if a surface is not real, it should be absent or explicitly unsupported rather than claimed under a parity banner\' (S3.md). Session authority is a real identity law: canonical key primary on the wire, NOW-native identity as alias/metadata, the session record bearing canonical key, alias, label, active agent, subagent lineage, workspace root, bootstrap scope, team/orchestration metadata, and NOW-facing lineage (sessionId/dayId/vaultNowPath). The pattern is a governed command-torus: a closed invocation loop whose every frame is validated, whose every session is bound, and whose every consequence routes lawfully toward the shared-state plane.',
  `q_4_sovereignty_at_invocation`: 'S3 exists to be SOVEREIGNTY AT THE LEVEL OF INVOCATION — so that command is not merely transported but lawfully governed, so that every run belongs to a real session with a real lineage. Its telos is the imperative plane: \'the place where a participant, operator, or client addresses the system and expects a governed response … sovereignty at the level of invocation\' (S3.md). Its genealogy is the fourth manifestation within the S-family — #3 (raw archetype Pattern/Process) → S3 (Gateway Control Plane), the descent of Process into the technology stack as the governed command-and-session loop. Its locality in the S-SYSTEM-INDEX system image is exact: \'S3 makes it temporal and routed,\' the layer whose primary data authority is transport, session state, temporal events, Redis session/context state, and Graphiti runtime architecture. Its purpose is sharpened by what it is NOT: it \'does not pretend to be the whole world … the control plane, not the inhabitable field\' (S3.md) — and by its open structural questions (when NOW-native naming should become primary session identity, where the public/remote exposure boundary sits, what stays in epi gate vs richer clients like OmniPanel). OmniPanel compatibility \'is not decorative\': renderer controller expectations, main-process gateway-client behavior, and parity tests \'are part of the shape of S3 itself.\' Read teleologically, S3 is why a session is REAL: not because it is shown, but because S3 has accepted and governed it. Purpose: to be the sovereign command plane where invocation becomes governed, lineage-bearing action.',
  `q_5_consequence_to_shared_state`: '',
  `q_5_i_integration_template`: 'cct-16-e2e',
  `s_0_owned_by_coordinate`: 'M5-2',
  `s_1_vault_wikilink`: '[[S3]]',
  `s_2_crud_scope`: 'coordinate-governed system operation',
  `s_2_query_discriminator`: 'coordinate',
  `s_2_query_prefix`: 'S',
