MATCH (n:Bimba {coordinate: 'S5'}) SET n += {
  `artifact_kind`: 'vault_markdown',
  `c_0_core_nature`: 'External APIs, sync, publication, automation, and world-facing execution boundary.',
  `c_1_description`: 'External crystallisation surface; Notion sync; publication and delivery; system presenting itself outward',
  `c_1_form`: 'Idea/Bimba/World/Types/Coordinates/S/S5/S5.md',
  `c_1_prior_description`: 'External APIs, sync, publication, automation, and world-facing execution boundary.',
  `c_1_prior_name`: 'Sync',
  `c_1_structure`: '{"authority_spec":"docs/specs/S/S5-S5i-SYNC.md","layer_name":"integral-world-boundary","promotion_contract":"s-branch-live-promotion-v1"}',
  `c_4_artifact_role`: 'definition',
  `content_hash`: 'sha256:26523b41b5b76470cadac1d5c7e92b575374c135c8071fc707296a09fe25c4c1',
  `coordinate_axis`: 'direct',
  `coordinate_depth`: 1,
  `coordinate_family`: 'S',
  `coordinate_kind`: 'root_direct',
  `coordinate_namespace`: 'S',
  `coordinate_parent`: 'S',
  `coordinate_prefix`: 'S5',
  `promotion_source`: 'pi_agent',
  `q_0_boundary_before_exchange`: 'Before S5 can exchange with the world it presupposes the whole inhabited stack that has something to send and somewhere to put what returns — S4\'s agentic work to crystallise, S3\'s transport to reach outward, S2\'s substrate to receive ingested corpus and episodic memory, S1\'s vault to hold the return, S0 to make any of it executable. As the S-family\'s manifestation of the raw #5 archetype (Integration/Pratibimba, CLAUDE.md II.A), S5\'s void-pole is the un-crossed boundary: the endpoint not yet called, the corpus not yet ingested, the publication not yet delivered, the world-return not yet folded back into ground — the bare fact of an outside the system has not yet addressed. \'S5 begins where those substrates become world-directed manifestation or world-return\' (S5.md): so S5\'s thrown ground is exactly the threshold before crossing, the addressability that precedes address. This boundary is double like every #5 (cf. C5/M5): it is the integral horizon the stack reaches toward (the world as that-which-exchange-is-with) AND the deeper return-condition it cannot author — that whatever goes out can come back enriched, that ingestion and reflection can become \'integral material for renewed action\' (S5.md). Before world-exchange, the boundary that consents to be crossed; before the Mobius returns, the outside that the system has located but not yet entered. S5\'s q_0 is the world-as-possibility: the integral edge held open before any exchange has yet made it actual.',
  `q_1_integral_world_boundary`: 'S5 IS the Integral World Boundary — \'the place where the stack stops being only internally coordinated and begins to participate in a wider field: external services, publication surfaces, notifications, webhook exchanges, public outputs, and the return currents that bring new material back into the system\' (S5.md). Against the other S-layers it is the one that \'makes it world-facing and reflective\' (S-SYSTEM-INDEX) — where S0 grounds, S1 resides, S2 stores, S3 governs, S4 inhabits, S5 RETURNS TO THE WORLD AND BACK. Its definitional substance is breadth corrected against two narrowings: \'S5 is not identical with Notion — Notion is one optional manifestation of this layer\' (S5.md), and the reduction of S5 to \'raw sync\' is \'too thin in the other direction.\' The canon that fits is: \'S5 is the world-boundary itself … defined by world exchange and return, not by any single vendor or protocol.\' It must be wide enough to encompass both eventual outward integrations (Notion, Telegram, n8n, email, generic webhooks — \'currently outward, partially implemented\') and \'the freshly implemented knowledge-return systems that already perform integral-world work in practice: Gnostic via RAG-Anything and Graphiti as episodic memory substrate\' (S5.md; CLAUDE.md II.C). Gnostic and Graphiti \'are not just S2 again … they are part of the world\'s return to the system: ingested corpus, lived history, and temporally qualified memory becoming available as integral material for renewed action.\' Definitionally S5 is the manifestation of #5 Integration in the technology stack: the outermost fold, world-exchange and world-return as one integral arc.',
  `q_2_exchange_and_return_operations`: '',
  `q_3_zero_sphere_world_edge`: '',
  `q_4_world_exchange_telos`: 'S5 exists to be the INTEGRAL WORLD-BOUNDARY — so that the system is not a closed loop but participates in a wider field and metabolises what that field returns. Its telos is world exchange and return (S5.md): \'the outermost fold of the stack: where the system meets the world, manifests into it, and receives the world\'s return.\' Its genealogy is the sixth and final manifestation within the S-family — #5 (raw archetype Integration/Pratibimba) → S5 (Integral World Boundary), the descent of Integration into the technology stack as the outward-and-inward arc. Its locality in the S-SYSTEM-INDEX is exact: \'S5 makes it world-facing and reflective,\' the layer whose primary data authority is world-return sources, M\' function outputs, crystallisation, improvement, review, and QL schema — and whose return spine is Epii: \'Epii is the return spine of Epi-Logos in reflection\' (S-SYSTEM-INDEX), governing review inbox, gnosis/kbase/Nara/Graphiti meaning-use, QL/MEF governance, and promotion decisions, distinct from Anima\'s dispatch spine. Its purpose is sharpened by the synthesis it holds open (S5.md): the old repo treated S5 as Notion/dashboard, the canonical plan as generic external API, the newest live implementation as Aletheia/Gnostic/Graphiti world-return — \'the synthesis taken here is therefore deliberate: S5 names the integral world-boundary, while specific implementation ownership remains distributed across adjacent modules.\' Read teleologically, S5 is why the system can learn from a world larger than itself: the boundary wide enough for what now exists \'without falsely relocating Gateway or SpacetimeDB out of S3/S3\'.\' Purpose: to be the integral edge where the stack manifests outward and the world\'s return becomes renewed ground.',
  `q_5_mobius_return_to_ground`: '',
  `s_0_owned_by_coordinate`: 'M5-2',
  `s_1_vault_wikilink`: '[[S5]]',
  `s_2_crud_scope`: 'world sync, recollection, improvement promotion',
  `s_2_query_discriminator`: 'coordinate',
  `s_2_query_prefix`: 'S',
  `s_4_function_role`: 'Direct S5 technical stack layer',
  `s_4_s5_agentic_protocol_owner`: 'M5-4',
  `s_5_runtime_use`: 'External crystallisation surface; Notion sync; publication and delivery; system presenting itself outward',
  `sync_status`: 'm5_s_lattice_integrated',
  `sync_version`: 'm5-s-lattice-migration-2026-06-03',
  `vault_path`: 'Idea/Bimba/World/Types/Coordinates/S/S5/S5.md'
};
