  `c_1_line_texts`: ['If one does not perpetuate the affair, there is little gossip. In the end, good fortune comes.', 'One cannot engage in conflict. One returns home, gives way. The people of his town, three hundred households, remain free of guilt.', 'To nourish oneself on ancient virtue induces perseverance. Danger. In the end, good fortune comes.', 'One cannot engage in conflict. One turns back and submits to fate.', 'To contend before him brings supreme good fortune.', 'Even if by chance a leather belt is bestowed on one, by the end of a morning it will have been snatched away three times.'],
