  `c_0_catalytic_nature`: 'The 1913 break energized Jung psychological crisis (1913-1916) leading to Red Book, active imagination, confrontation with unconscious, and all subsequent discoveries',
  `c_0_operational_essence`: 'Creative wound and generative rupture - the break that traumatized yet birthed a new psychological paradigm',
  `c_1_consciousness_structure`: 'Pre-theoretical lived crisis exemplifying archetypal separation pattern - the hero must kill the father to individuate',
  `c_1_internal_structure`: 'Contains four catalytic controversies as internal tensions: Libido Theory (sexual determinism vs generalized life force), Unconscious Structure (personal repressed vs collective archetypal), Teleology (past causation vs future finality), Religious Attitude (reduction vs amplification). These oppositions energized Jung entire subsequent work.',
  `c_1_operational_symbolics`: '',
