MATCH (n:Bimba {coordinate: 'M4.4.3-2'}) SET n += {
  `c_0_operational_essence`: 'Psychic energy (libido) flowing along gradients created by tensions, regulated by compensation, structured by complexes, manifesting synchronistically',
  `c_1_consciousness_structure`: 'The felt dynamics of psychic life - motivation, conflict, automatic regulation, possession by complexes, meaningful coincidences',
  `c_1_internal_structure`: 'Contains six dimensions of efficient causation: libido as primordial life force and source-energy, undifferentiated power manifesting as sexuality-creativity-spirituality depending on channels, Spanda gathering in-breath (2-0); opposites generating tension creating potential energy through polarization, fundamental oppositions like consciousness-unconscious, ego-shadow, thinking-feeling as generative not pathological (2-1); compensation as self-regulating mechanism where unconscious automatically corrects conscious one-sidedness through dreams and symptoms (2-2); shadow as autonomous force containing both denied negativity and undeveloped positive potentials, gold in darkness acting against ego will (2-3); complexes as emotionally-charged organizing nuclei structured around archetypal cores, autonomous sub-personalities temporarily possessing consciousness (2-4); synchronicity as acausal meaningful connection transcending mechanical causation, psychoid interface where psyche-matter reveal unified ground, Spanda dispersal out-breath (2-5). Architecture shows energy gathering inward (libido), generating through opposition, self-regulating through compensation, crystallizing in autonomous structures (shadow, complexes), dispersing outward through synchronistic connection.',
  `c_1_operational_symbolics`: 'Energy flow and blockage, shadow projection, complex activation, synchronistic connection, Spanda in-breath and out-breath',
  `c_2_id`: '4.3-2',
  `c_2_notion_page_id`: '1d2a4797-123c-8180-9be9-f3f350454be5',
  `c_4_architectural_function`: 'Establishes how psychological events actually occur - the energic mechanisms generating symptoms, dreams, emotions, projections, synchronicities. Not mechanical causation but energic flow and acausal orderedness.',
  `c_4_layer`: 'COORDINATE',
  `c_4_ontological_layer`: 'Epistemology (How/Knowing)',
  `c_4_subsystem`: 4,
  `l_4_jungian_concept`: 'Synchronicity, Archetype/Image Distinction, Shadow, Mythology, Astrology'
};
MATCH (n:Bimba {coordinate: 'M4.4.3-2-0'}) SET n += {
  `c_0_operational_essence`: '',
  `c_1_consciousness_structure`: '',
  `c_1_internal_structure`: '',
  `c_1_operational_symbolics`: '',
  `c_3_source_energy`: '',
  `c_4_architectural_function`: '',
  `c_4_energic_viewpoint`: 'Jung distinguished mechanistic-causal (tracing effects back to past causes, Freud approach) from energic-final (understanding energy flow along gradients toward goals, Jung approach). At position 0 we are at energic source.',
  `c_4_equivalence_entropy`: 'Equivalence principle: if energy decreases in one area appears in another (conservation). Entropy principle: energy distribution seeks equilibrium (self-regulation). Gradient flow: energy follows potential differences toward goals.',
  `c_4_layer`: 'COORDINATE',
  `c_4_subsystem`: 4,
  `l_4_spanda_in_breath`: '',
  `t_4_created`: ''
};
MATCH (n:Bimba {coordinate: 'M4.4.3-2-1'}) SET n += {
  `c_0_operational_essence`: 'Polarity creating potential energy - greater tension generates more energy available for transformation',
  `c_1_consciousness_structure`: 'The shuttle between thesis-antithesis generating synthetic energy',
  `c_1_internal_structure`: 'Jung discovery: shuttling to and fro of arguments and affects represents transcendent function of opposites. Confrontation of two positions generates tension charged with energy, creates living third thing. Key oppositions in Jungian psychology: consciousness-unconscious (fundamental split creating psychic space), ego-shadow (personal identity vs denied aspects), thinking-feeling (truth-judgment vs value-judgment), sensation-intuition (concrete vs abstract perception), introversion-extraversion (interior vs exterior orientation), anima-animus (feminine in masculine and vice versa), persona-authentic self (social mask vs genuine being). Each opposition creates potential energy - greater tension, more energy available for transformation when resolution occurs.',
  `c_1_operational_symbolics`: 'Electrical poles, alchemical sulphur-mercury, yang-yin, positive-negative charges',
  `c_4_architectural_function`: 'Shows how source-energy (libido) becomes active force through opposition. After source-energy at position 0, position 1 shows energy activation mechanism.',
  `c_4_layer`: 'COORDINATE',
  `c_4_subsystem`: 4,
  `c_4_tension_generation`: 'Mechanism through which libido becomes active. Without opposition libido remains potential; through opposition becomes kinetic producing dreams, symptoms, emotions, actions, insights.',
  `c_4_transcendent_potential`: 'How holding tension enables transformation. Not resolving opposites prematurely but sustaining paradox until third emerges.',
  `p_4_key_oppositions`: 'Consciousness-unconscious, ego-shadow, thinking-feeling, sensation-intuition, introversion-extraversion, anima-animus, persona-authentic self. Each opposition creates potential energy.',
  `p_4_opposition_principle`: 'How polarity creates potential energy. Like electrical current requiring positive-negative poles, psychic energy requires polarized opposites.',
  `t_4_created`: '2025-10-09T20:50:30.403000000Z'
};
