MATCH (n:Bimba {coordinate: 'M4.4.3-2-3'}) SET n += {
  `c_0_operational_essence`: 'Unconscious motivation producing life effects through compulsion, projection, self-sabotage',
  `c_1_consciousness_structure`: 'What we do not bring to consciousness appears in our lives as fate',
  `c_1_internal_structure`: 'Jung definition: shadow is hidden, repressed, for most part inferior and guilt-laden personality whose ultimate ramifications reach back into realm of our animal ancestors. But also contains: normal instincts, appropriate reactions, realistic insights, creative impulses that consciousness rejected. Shadow does not wait for permission - acts behind our own back through: addictions (shadow compulsion), emotional outbursts (shadow overwhelms ego-control), self-sabotage (shadow undermines conscious goals), projections (shadow seen in others not self).',
  `c_1_operational_symbolics`: 'Dark twin, hidden other, Mr. Hyde, repressed animal nature, denied gold',
  `c_4_architectural_function`: 'At cycle midpoint represents maximal autonomous opposition. Where oppositions and compensations crystallize into quasi-independent sub-personality acting against ego intentions.',
  `c_4_autonomous_motivation`: 'Shadow as independent force operating unconsciously. When Jung said what we do not bring to consciousness appears in our lives as fate, he meant shadow AS efficient cause producing effects through unconscious motivation.',
  `c_4_layer`: 'COORDINATE',
  `c_4_negative_positive_polarity`: 'Shadow is not only negative. Often contains: healthy aggression denied by nice persona, creative wildness denied by conformist ego, authentic spontaneity denied by controlled facade, instinctual wisdom denied by over-rationality. Gold in darkness.',
  `c_4_projection_mechanism`: 'Shadow typically seen in others before recognized in self. What we hate in others is often our own denied shadow projected outward.',
  `c_4_subsystem`: 4,
  `t_3_integration_process`: 'Shadow work releases trapped libido - energy working against ego becomes available for individuation. Recognition not elimination - this is me too.',
  `t_4_created`: '2025-10-09T20:50:30.403000000Z'
};
MATCH (n:Bimba {coordinate: 'M4.4.3-2-4'}) SET n += {
  `c_0_operational_essence`: 'Channeling structures for libido organizing around specific themes creating behavioral patterns',
  `c_1_consciousness_structure`: 'When complex activates, temporarily possesses consciousness - no longer acting from ego-center but complex-center',
  `c_1_internal_structure`: 'Structure of complexes: archetypal core (universal pattern like Mother, Father, Hero, Anima-Animus), personal experiences (specific biographical content clustering around core), emotional charge (affects disproportionate to situation), autonomous behavior (acts independently often against ego). Example: mother complex = Mother archetype + experiences with personal mother + emotional charge → behaves like independent sub-personality affecting all relationships with women, authority, nurture. Discovery through word-association test measuring response time and physiological changes to stimulus words - delayed responses, emotional reactions, memory gaps indicated complexes.',
  `c_1_operational_symbolics`: 'Planetary nodes pulling consciousness, emotional magnets, autonomous sub-personalities',
  `c_1_structured_energy`: 'How complexes organize libido around archetypal cores creating behavioral patterns. Channeling structures for psychic energy organizing around specific themes.',
  `c_1_word_association_empirics`: 'Jung developed word-association test as scientific discovery method. Measure response time and physiological changes to stimulus words. Delayed responses, emotional reactions, memory gaps indicated complexes.',
  `c_4_archetype_personal_link`: 'Complexes as personal instantiation of universal archetypal patterns. Archetype-as-such at position 0-3, complex at position 2-4 is personal manifestation, archetypal image is conscious representation.',
  `c_4_architectural_function`: 'Represents structured channeling of psychic energy. After shadow as diffuse opposition, complexes show energy organized into specific patterns around archetypal cores.',
  `c_4_autonomous_action`: 'Complexes temporarily possess ego-consciousness. When complex activates, no longer acting from ego-center but complex-center. You are taken over.',
  `c_4_layer`: 'COORDINATE',
  `c_4_subsystem`: 4,
  `t_4_created`: '2025-10-09T20:50:30.403000000Z'
};
MATCH (n:Bimba {coordinate: 'M4.4.3-2-5'}) SET n += {
  `c_0_operational_essence`: 'Acausal connection through meaning - effect without mechanical cause, Spanda dispersal phase',
  `c_1_consciousness_structure`: 'Individual-cosmic connection, synchronistic recognition as pratyabhijna at cosmic scale',
  `c_1_internal_structure`: 'Jung definition: acausal connecting principle linking events through meaning rather than causation. Classic example: patient dreams of golden scarab beetle, actual scarab taps Jung window at that moment - no causal connection but profound meaning. Psychoid level: synchronicity emerges from psychoid interface where psyche and matter indistinguishable. At deepest level no psyche-matter split, only unus mundus. Synchronicity is unified reality manifesting experientially. Jung-Pauli collaboration: dual-aspect monism (psyche and matter two aspects of psychophysically neutral reality), complementarity (consciousness-unconscious complementary like wave-particle), acausal orderedness (pattern-making tendency predating physical laws).',
  `c_1_operational_symbolics`: 'The out-breath, projection outward, individual meeting collective, psyche touching matter',
  `c_4_acausal_connection`: 'Meaningful coincidence without mechanical causation. Internal psychological event corresponds to external physical event through significance not causality. Patient dreams scarab, actual scarab appears - no cause but profound meaning.',
  `c_4_architectural_function`: 'Represents transcendence of mechanical efficient causation. At cycle culmination, efficient cause reveals itself as not requiring mechanical chains - meaning connects psyche-matter directly.',
  `c_4_complexity_emergence`: 'Modern research shows synchronicity as emergent self-organization in complex adaptive systems. Non-linear causality producing moments of complexity transforming system states. Jung intuition scientifically validated.',
  `c_4_layer`: 'COORDINATE',
  `c_4_subsystem`: 4,
  `l_4_spanda_out_breath`: 'Dispersal, radiating, moving-toward-periphery phase. Where libido at position 0 is gathering in-breath, synchronicity at position 5 is dispersal out-breath. Energy radiating outward connecting individual to collective.',
  `s_4_psychoid_interface`: 'Synchronicity emerges from psychoid interface where psyche-matter indistinguishable. At deepest level no split, only unus mundus. Synchronicity is unified reality manifesting experientially.',
  `t_4_created`: '2025-10-09T20:50:30.403000000Z'
};
MATCH (n:Bimba {coordinate: 'M4.4.3-3'}) SET n += {
  `c_0_operational_essence`: 'Formal transformation through structured dissolution and integration following archetypal pattern',
  `c_1_consciousness_structure`: 'Crisis-confusion requiring transformation, progressive clarification through stages, method for conscious engagement',
  `c_1_internal_structure`: 'Contains six dimensions of formal transformation: prima materia as structured chaos, deterministic chaos with strange attractors, alpha-omega identity (beginning-end same substance transformed), chaos theory isomorphism with phase transitions (3-0); nigredo as blackening-dissolution, formal pattern of breaking down, shadow confrontation, necessary death preceding rebirth, depression as alchemical stage not only pathology (3-1); albedo as whitening-purification, formal pattern of discernment separating essence from dross, anima-animus work, moonlight indirect knowing through reflection (3-2); citrinitas as yellowing-illumination, formal pattern of recognition and sudden insight, solar direct knowing, first integration as dawn before full day, pratyabhijna breakthrough (3-3); rubedo as reddening-completion, formal pattern of embodied wholeness, coniunctio oppositorum uniting opposites in differentiated unity, philosopher stone as individuated personality, provisional not permanent completion (3-4); transcendent function as formal method, dialectical thesis-antithesis-synthesis structure, active imagination technique with four steps, conscious participation in unconscious process, wu wei paradox (3-5). Architecture shows transformation beginning from confusion (prima materia) through progressive stages to provisional completion, with method enabling conscious participation rather than passive undergoing.',
  `c_1_operational_symbolics`: 'Alchemical opus, blackening-whitening-yellowing-reddening, coniunctio oppositorum, philosopher stone, transcendent function',
  `c_2_id`: '4.3-3',
  `c_2_notion_page_id`: '1d2a4797-123c-81ea-a3c5-c5f929f25647',
  `c_4_architectural_function`: 'Establishes the formal patterns through which psychological transformation occurs - not mechanical steps but archetypal stages recognized across psychotherapy, spiritual development, creative process, life transitions.',
  `c_4_layer`: 'COORDINATE',
  `c_4_ontological_layer`: 'Psychology (Mediating Structure)',
  `c_4_subsystem`: 4,
  `l_4_jungian_concept`: 'Alchemy, Individuation, Transcendent Function, Active Imagination'
};
MATCH (n:Bimba {coordinate: 'M4.4.3-3-0'}) SET n += {
  `c_0_operational_essence`: 'Structured chaos containing formal attractors of its own reorganization - gold in the dung',
  `c_1_consciousness_structure`: 'The chaotic givenness of thrown existence demanding we make sense through formal engagement',
  `c_1_internal_structure`: 'Jung identification: prima materia is the unconscious itself. But at formal cause domain, we see unconscious not as primordial source but as that which requires formal transformation, as chaos demanding pattern, as confused state necessitating opus. Van Eenwyk chaos dynamics insight: prima materia has deterministic chaos with strange attractors (deep structures organizing psychic chaos into recognizable patterns), fractal self-similarity (same patterns at different scales), bifurcation points (critical thresholds where small changes produce large effects), sensitive dependence (initial conditions determining divergent developmental paths), iteration (repetitive processes generating complex patterns from simple rules).',
  `c_1_operational_symbolics`: 'The dung, the nigredo before nigredo, the confused mess, deterministic chaos, strange attractors',
  `c_1_structured_chaos`: 'Prima materia is not formless void but deterministic chaos. Van Eenwyk: What seems chaotic is much healthier than commonly supposed. Healthy psyche has deterministic chaos with underlying patterns.',
  `c_2_alpha_omega_identity`: 'Beginning and end are same substance - prima materia at start contains gold, opus makes this explicit. Must circle through stages to recognize what was always present.',
  `c_4_architectural_function`: 'Establishes alpha-omega identity at formal level. Where alchemical work begins (confused chaotic state) and where it returns (same material now recognized as containing gold all along). Void-position at formal cause requiring circumambulation.',
  `c_4_chaos_theoretic_isomorphism`: 'Psychic transformation follows thermodynamic phase transitions: nigredo (far from equilibrium dissolution), albedo (separation of elements purification), citrinitas (emergence of new order), rubedo (new stable attractor). Not metaphor but isomorphism.',
  `c_4_layer`: 'COORDINATE',
  `c_4_strange_attractors`: 'Deep formal structures organizing psychic chaos into recognizable patterns. Attractors are formal principles pulling system toward certain states despite surface randomness.',
  `c_4_subsystem`: 4,
  `t_4_created`: '2025-10-09T20:50:30.403000000Z'
};
MATCH (n:Bimba {coordinate: 'M4.4.3-3-1'}) SET n += {
  `c_0_operational_essence`: 'Increasing entropy, moving system far from equilibrium through structured dissolution',
  `c_1_consciousness_structure`: 'Depression, despair, meaninglessness as formal stages not pathological failures',
  `c_1_internal_structure`: 'Formal pattern of breaking down appears as: depression and despair (loss of meaning), confronting shadow aspects denied, death of ego-identifications (who I thought I was), loss of meaning-structures that once worked, dark night of soul. Why necessary: cannot skip to albedo purification without nigredo dissolution. Old structures must decompose before new can form. Like composting - rotting is necessary stage for fertility. Blackening is not failure but prerequisite. Jung personal nigredo: 1913-1916 crisis following Freud break, near-psychotic episode, visions of destruction, confrontation with unconscious figures. Red Book emerges from nigredo - darkness IS the material.',
  `c_1_operational_symbolics`: 'The blackening, putrefaction, rotting, composting, death as prerequisite for rebirth',
  `c_4_across_domains`: 'Nigredo pattern appears in: psychotherapy (initial phase where defenses break down), spiritual practice (dark night confronting void), creative process (confusion blockage before breakthrough), life transitions (divorce, career loss, identity crisis).',
  `c_4_architectural_function`: 'Establishes formal pattern of breaking down. Not random destruction but structured dissolution - separating fused elements, destroying false unities, returning composite to constituent parts.',
  `c_4_dissolution_pattern`: 'Formal structure of breaking down and decomposing. Separating fused elements, destroying false unities, returning composite to constituents. In chaos terms: increasing entropy, moving far from equilibrium.',
  `c_4_layer`: 'COORDINATE',
  `c_4_necessary_death`: 'Cannot skip nigredo. Old structures must decompose before new can form. Like composting - rotting is necessary stage for fertility. Blackening is not failure but prerequisite.',
  `c_4_shadow_confrontation`: 'Psychological manifestation as meeting denied aspects, death of ego-identifications, loss of meaning-structures that once worked. Confronting what was repressed.',
  `c_4_subsystem`: 4,
  `t_4_created`: '2025-10-09T20:50:30.403000000Z'
};
MATCH (n:Bimba {coordinate: 'M4.4.3-3-2'}) SET n += {
  `c_0_operational_essence`: 'Selective amplification of certain patterns while dampening others through discernment',
  `c_1_consciousness_structure`: 'Clarifying what matters from what seemed important, washing away ego-inflation and false identifications',
  `c_1_internal_structure`: 'Formal pattern of discernment manifests as: distinguishing true self from false personas, anima work for men (relating consciously to inner feminine), animus work for women (relating consciously to inner masculine), washing away ego-inflation grandiosity false identifications, clarifying what matters from what seemed important. Washing metaphor: alchemical texts describe repeated washings (ablutio) - rinsing away impurities. Psychologically each washing removes layer of unconscious identification. Recognize I am not my anger, not my success, not what others think - each recognition purifies. Moonlight versus sunlight: albedo associated with moon - reflected light not direct. This is indirect knowing, seeing through reflection rather than confronting directly. Anima-animus serve as reflective mediators between ego and deeper Self.',
  `c_1_operational_symbolics`: 'The washing, moonlight reflected knowing, silver queen, Luna, purification through repeated rinsing',
  `c_4_anima_animus_work`: 'Psychological manifestation as conscious relationship to contrasexual other. Anima work (for men) relating to inner feminine, animus work (for women) relating to inner masculine. These serve as reflective mediators.',
  `c_4_architectural_function`: 'Establishes formal pattern of discernment. After dissolution now discrimination - this is essential, that is accidental; this serves wholeness, that fragments.',
  `c_4_indirect_knowing`: 'Moonlight consciousness - reflected light not direct. Seeing through reflection rather than confronting directly. Anima-animus as mirrors reflecting between ego and Self.',
  `c_4_layer`: 'COORDINATE',
  `c_4_purification_pattern`: 'Formal structure of separating essence from dross. After dissolution (nigredo) now discrimination - this essential, that accidental; this serves wholeness, that fragments. In chaos terms: selective amplification.',
  `c_4_subsystem`: 4,
  `t_3_clarification_process`: 'How confusion gradually resolves into discernment. Each washing removes layer of unconscious identification. Gradual clarification of what truly matters from what seemed important.',
  `t_4_created`: '2025-10-09T20:50:30.403000000Z'
};
MATCH (n:Bimba {coordinate: 'M4.4.3-3-3'}) SET n += {
  `c_0_operational_essence`: 'Emergence of new order from chaos through self-organization manifesting as recognition',
  `c_1_consciousness_structure`: 'Sudden insights, I finally see, breakthrough moments where pattern crystallizes',
  `c_1_internal_structure`: 'Formal pattern of recognition manifests as: sudden insights (I finally see), integration of conscious and unconscious beginning, solar consciousness (direct knowing not reflected versus albedo lunar), first glimpse of Self as organizing center, numinous quality (sense of sacred and profound). Solar transition: moving from albedo (lunar reflected) to citrinitas (solar direct) marks crucial threshold. Indirect knowing through anima-animus mediation becomes direct knowing through self-evident recognition. Like sun breaking through clouds. Why sometimes omitted: some alchemical texts use three-stage opus (nigredo-albedo-rubedo) folding citrinitas into rubedo. Why? Because citrinitas is transitional - first light before full day (rubedo). It is dawn not noon.',
  `c_1_operational_symbolics`: 'Dawn breaking, sun rising, golden yellow, solar consciousness direct knowing, the aha moment',
  `c_4_architectural_function`: 'Establishes formal pattern of recognition. After dissolution and purification now synthesis begins - seeing the whole, the aha moment, pratyabhijna recognition.',
  `c_4_layer`: 'COORDINATE',
  `c_4_numinous_quality`: 'Sacred dimension of breakthrough moments. Sense of profound, numinous, holy. Recognition has quality of revelation not mere intellectual understanding.',
  `c_4_recognition_pattern`: 'Formal structure of sudden insight and seeing-through. After dissolution and purification now synthesis begins - seeing whole, aha moment, pratyabhijna recognition. In chaos terms: emergence of new order, self-organization.',
  `c_4_solar_direct`: 'Transition from reflected to direct knowing. Albedo is lunar (indirect through anima-animus mediation), citrinitas is solar (direct self-evident recognition). Sun breaking through clouds.',
  `c_4_subsystem`: 4,
  `c_5_first_integration`: 'Beginning of conscious-unconscious synthesis. First glimpse of Self as organizing center. Integration commencing not yet complete (that is rubedo).',
  `t_4_created`: '2025-10-09T20:50:30.403000000Z'
};
MATCH (n:Bimba {coordinate: 'M4.4.3-3-4'}) SET n += {
  `c_0_operational_essence`: 'New stable attractor basin achieved, system reorganized at higher complexity maintaining far-from-equilibrium order',
  `c_1_consciousness_structure`: 'The Self as lived reality not concept, incarnate wisdom not knowing about but knowing as',
  `c_1_internal_structure`: 'Formal pattern of embodied wholeness manifests as: conscious-unconscious integrated (not merged but differentiated unity), opposites reconciled (thinking-feeling, sensation-intuition, masculine-feminine), Self as lived reality not concept, incarnate wisdom (not knowing about but knowing as), philosopher stone as individuated personality. Reddening symbolizes blood, life, embodiment. Where citrinitas is insight (mental), rubedo is incarnation (somatic). Realization must descend into body, daily life, relationships. Otherwise abstract knowledge not transformation. Coniunctio oppositorum (conjunction of opposites) is rubedo essence - not eliminating opposition but integrating: Rex and Regina (masculine-feminine), Sol and Luna (consciousness-unconscious), Sulphur and Salt (active-passive), Spirit and Matter (psyche-soma). Coniunctio produces philosopher stone - synthesized personality. Why not final: Jung insisted individuation is not achieved once-for-all. Rubedo represents provisional completion - genuine but not permanent. Philosopher stone achieved in one cycle becomes prima materia for next. The Möbius return: rubedo returns to prima materia now enriched.',
  `c_1_operational_symbolics`: 'The reddening, blood life embodiment, philosopher stone, red king, coniunctio oppositorum',
  `c_4_architectural_function`: 'Establishes formal pattern of embodied wholeness. After dissolution, purification, illumination now integration actualizes in lived reality.',
  `c_4_completion_pattern`: 'Formal structure of integration and wholeness achieved. After dissolution, purification, illumination now actualizing in lived reality. In chaos terms: new stable attractor basin, system reorganized at higher complexity.',
  `c_4_coniunctio_oppositorum`: 'Reconciliation of polarities in differentiated unity. Not eliminating opposites but integrating: Rex-Regina, Sol-Luna, Sulphur-Salt, Spirit-Matter. Coniunctio produces philosopher stone (individuated personality).',
  `c_4_layer`: 'COORDINATE',
  `c_4_provisional_stability`: 'Genuine completion but not permanent. Jung insisted individuation not achieved once-for-all. Rubedo is provisional completion opening to new cycle. Philosopher stone becomes prima materia for next transformation.',
  `c_4_subsystem`: 4,
  `l_4_embodiment_necessity`: 'Why insight must incarnate in lived reality. Citrinitas is mental insight, rubedo is somatic incarnation. Must descend into body, daily life, relationships. Otherwise abstract knowledge not transformation.',
  `t_4_created`: '2025-10-09T20:50:30.403000000Z'
};
MATCH (n:Bimba {coordinate: 'M4.4.3-3-5'}) SET n += {
  `c_0_operational_essence`: 'Conscious participation in unconscious process through dialectical engagement - wu wei at formal level',
  `c_1_consciousness_structure`: 'The capacity to hold opposites in tension until third emerges transcending both',
  `c_1_dialectical_structure`: 'Thesis-antithesis-synthesis as formal pattern. Jung used mathematical language explicitly: psychological function comparable to mathematical function operating on real (conscious) and imaginary (unconscious) numbers producing complex number (synthesis).',
  `c_1_internal_structure`: 'Transcendent function as formal structure: Jung explicitly used mathematical language (psychological function comparable to mathematical function of same name operating on real and imaginary numbers). Formal pattern: thesis (conscious attitude as real number), antithesis (unconscious compensation as imaginary number), synthesis (new third position transcending both as complex number). Not arbitrary metaphor but mathematical isomorphism operating on psychic numbers. Active imagination as method for activating transcendent function - four formal steps: empty conscious mind (create formal space, receptive void), let unconscious images arise (allow formal content to emerge spontaneously), observe without interference (maintain formal witnessing position), engage in dialogue (enter formal dialectical relationship). Not passive fantasy but active engagement - hence active imagination. Ego participates consciously in unconscious process.',
  `c_1_operational_symbolics`: '',
  `c_4_active_imagination_method`: '',
  `c_4_architectural_function`: '',
  `c_4_layer`: 'COORDINATE',
  `c_4_multiple_containers`: 'Different media sharing same formal structure: visualization (seeing inner figures landscapes), narrative (dialoguing with personifications), embodied movement (dance gesture expressing unconscious), visual art (painting sculpting from unconscious), music (playing composing from depth).',
  `c_4_paradoxical_engagement`: 'Active imagination embodies wu wei (action through non-action). Active: ego maintains consciousness, does not drift. Imagination: allows unconscious autonomy, does not control. Paradox is formal structure - conscious participation in unconscious process.',
  `c_4_subsystem`: 4,
  `t_4_created`: '2025-10-09T20:50:30.403000000Z'
};
MATCH (n:Bimba {coordinate: 'M4.4.3-4'}) SET n += {
  `c_0_operational_essence`: 'Teleological organization through meaning - wholeness as already-present yet to-be-realized drawing development',
  `c_1_consciousness_structure`: 'The Self as both immanent (always already here as ground) and transcendent (goal never fully reached), circumambulation rather than linear progression',
  `c_1_internal_structure`: 'Contains six dimensions of Self as telos: Self as context, horizonal wholeness structuring perception without being perceived, anuttara unsurpassable transcendental condition, the field within which ego operates like figure against ground (4.0); Self as organizing center, focal point around which psyche organizes maintaining coherence, mandala center, axis mundi, what circumambulation circles around (4.1); Self as totality, complete circumference embracing conscious and unconscious, ego and shadow, all opposites in coincidentia oppositorum, radical inclusivity with indeterminate extent merging into collective (4.2); mandala as spontaneous symbol, Self self-representation emerging during disorientation, quaternity structure (circle plus four), compensatory function reorienting fragmented consciousness, archetypal mathematics made visible (4.3); circumambulation as process, spiral not linear development, returning to same point transformed at higher level, process IS telos, toroidal necessity requiring ongoing circulation (4.4); Self as actual unity, achieved wholeness and transcendence, conscious realization moving from potential to actual, gnosis as direct knowing through being not knowing about, provisional completion opening to new cycle (4.5). Architecture shows Self as simultaneously ground (context), goal (center and totality), guide (mandala symbol), path (circumambulation), and achievement (actual unity), resolving into Möbius where achievement returns to ground enriched.',
  `c_1_operational_symbolics`: 'Mandala quaternity, circumference and center, axis mundi, circumambulation, philosopher stone, coniunctio',
  `c_2_id`: '4.3-4',
  `c_2_notion_page_id`: '1d2a4797-123c-8161-b793-db2aacf3396b',
  `c_4_architectural_function`: 'Establishes the telos of Jungian psychology - wholeness as goal that already exists requiring recognition not creation. Self organizing development without determining path, drawing consciousness toward integration.',
  `c_4_layer`: 'COORDINATE',
  `c_4_ontological_layer`: 'Contextual Domain (Flowering)',
  `c_4_subsystem`: 4,
  `l_4_jungian_concept`: 'Self Archetype Expression, Mandala Symbolism'
};
MATCH (n:Bimba {coordinate: 'M4.4.3-4.0'}) SET n += {
  `c_0_operational_essence`: 'Horizonal wholeness structuring perception without being perceived - anuttara at psychological level',
  `c_1_consciousness_structure`: 'The always-already-there field within which consciousness operates, implicit wholeness preceding ego-awareness',
  `c_1_contextual_field`: 'Self as situation and horizon rather than object. Not psychological content but formal structure enabling contents to appear, cohere, mean. Context within which all psychological life occurs.',
  `c_1_internal_structure`: 'Jung: Self is not only center but also whole circumference embracing both conscious and unconscious. At position 0 we emphasize Self as circumference, as total context, as that which cannot be grasped directly because it is very condition of grasping. Anuttara quality: position 0 corresponds to Anuttara in Kashmir Shaivism (unsurpassable, beyond categories, transcendental condition). Self-as-context is Anuttara at psychological level - can never step outside it to observe because it is field within which observation occurs. Contextuality connection: position 4 in framework corresponds to contextuality where patterns flower in specific situations. Self as context represents wholeness as situation within which ego operates. Ego does not exist in isolation but always within Self field, like figure against ground.',
  `c_1_operational_symbolics`: 'The circumference, horizon, context, field, ground, unus mundus at psychic level',
  `c_4_anuttara_quality`: 'Unsurpassable, beyond categories, transcendental condition. Can never step outside Self to observe because it is field within which observation occurs. Anuttara at psychological level.',
  `c_4_architectural_function`: 'Establishes Self as circumference at position 4 telos domain. Not Self as center-point but as horizonal field, unsurpassable context, the thrown situation within which ego operates.',
  `c_4_horizonal_wholeness`: 'That which structures perception without being perceived. Husserl concept of horizon - not object but boundary-structure enabling perception. Self-as-context functions identically.',
  `c_4_implicit_totality`: 'Pre-reflective wholeness preceding ego-consciousness. Most people never consciously encounter Self as object yet live within its field. Neurotic is one who lost touch with Self-as-context - fragmentation because horizonal wholeness collapsed.',
  `c_4_layer`: 'COORDINATE',
  `c_4_subsystem`: 4,
  `t_4_created`: '2025-10-09T20:50:30.403000000Z'
};
MATCH (n:Bimba {coordinate: 'M4.4.3-4.1'}) SET n += {
  `c_0_operational_essence`: 'The point organizing psychic contents into coherent personality - seed point crystallizing structure',
  `c_1_consciousness_structure`: 'Goal of individuation, organizing principle already operative, point of maximum stability',
  `c_1_internal_structure`: 'Organizing function: like crystal seed point organizing solution into structure, Self-as-center organizes psychic contents into coherent personality. Without this organizing center: dissociation (multiple sub-personalities without integration), fragmentation (thoughts emotions behaviors lacking coherence), identity diffusion (no stable sense of I). Self organizing function is not conscious control (that is ego) but deeper structural principle maintaining integrity. Mandala central point: Jung discovery - mandalas spontaneously appearing in dreams and art during crises feature central point as Self-symbol. Center represents: goal of individuation, organizing principle already operative, point of maximum stability, intersection of opposites (vertical-horizontal axes). Circumambulation around center: there is no linear evolution; there is only circumambulation of self. Development does not progress away from origin toward goal but circles around center, spiraling closer through repeated cycles. Each circumambulation brings deeper recognition of center that was always there.',
  `c_1_operational_symbolics`: '',
  `c_4_architectural_function`: '',
  `c_4_circumambulation_axis`: 'What development circles around rather than progresses toward. There is no linear evolution; only circumambulation of self. Development does not progress away from origin but circles around center, spiraling closer through repeated cycles.',
  `c_4_layer`: 'COORDINATE',
  `c_4_mandala_center`: '',
  `c_4_organizing_principle`: 'How Self-as-center maintains psychic coherence. Like crystal seed organizing solution into structure. Without organizing center: dissociation, fragmentation, identity diffusion. Self organizing function not conscious control but deeper structural principle.',
  `c_4_subsystem`: 4,
  `c_4_teleological_focus`: 'Point development aims toward. While Self-as-context (position 0) is field you are in, Self-as-center (position 1) is point you are moving toward. But paradoxically, since already in field, moving toward center is recognizing where you have always been.',
  `t_4_created`: '2025-10-09T20:50:30.403000000Z'
};
MATCH (n:Bimba {coordinate: 'M4.4.3-4.2'}) SET n += {
  `c_0_operational_essence`: 'Radical inclusivity - nothing excluded, all opposites held in differentiated unity',
  `c_1_consciousness_structure`: 'Wholeness as goal toward which all development aims yet which already exists implicitly',
  `c_1_internal_structure`: 'What is included in Self-as-totality: ego-consciousness (small but necessary perspective), shadow (denied repressed aspects), anima-animus (contrasexual dimensions), personal unconscious (biographical material), collective unconscious (archetypal patterns), transcendent function (capacity to hold opposites). Nothing excluded - Self AS totality is radical inclusivity. Coincidentia oppositorum: Nicholas of Cusa term adopted by Jung for union of opposites. Not eliminating opposites or resolving into neutral middle but holding both in tension within higher unity: conscious and unconscious (not merged, integrated), good and evil (not moralistic splitting, ethical totality), masculine and feminine (not androgyny, differentiated wholeness), light and dark (not elimination of shadow, conscious inclusion). Self is bright and dark and yet neither - transcends while including opposites. Von Franz elaboration: Self embraces ego-consciousness, shadow, anima, collective unconscious in indeterminable extension. The indeterminable is crucial - can never fully circumscribe Self extent because merges imperceptibly with unus mundus, collective unconscious, reality itself.',
  `c_1_operational_symbolics`: 'The complete circle, mandala circumference, uroboros, cosmic egg, pleroma',
  `c_2_coincidentia_oppositorum`: 'Union of opposites in differentiated unity. Not eliminating or resolving but holding in tension within higher unity: conscious-unconscious integrated not merged, good-evil ethical totality not moralistic splitting, masculine-feminine differentiated wholeness not androgyny, light-dark conscious inclusion not shadow elimination.',
  `c_4_architectural_function`: 'Establishes complete end-state at telos level. Where Self-as-center is focal point, Self-as-totality is entire circle. Yet paradoxically totality already exists - individuation does not create but recognizes.',
  `c_4_holistic_telos`: 'Wholeness as goal toward which all development aims. Yet paradoxically wholeness already exists - individuation recognizes what was always present rather than creating new totality.',
  `c_4_indeterminate_extent`: 'Von Franz: Self embraces in indeterminable extension. Cannot fully circumscribe Self extent because merges imperceptibly with unus mundus, collective unconscious, reality itself. Self has no clear boundary separating from cosmos.',
  `c_4_layer`: 'COORDINATE',
  `c_4_radical_inclusivity`: 'Self as containing all aspects without exception. Ego-consciousness, shadow, anima-animus, personal unconscious, collective unconscious, transcendent function. Nothing excluded - radical inclusivity.',
  `c_4_subsystem`: 4,
  `t_4_created`: '2025-10-09T20:50:30.403000000Z'
};
MATCH (n:Bimba {coordinate: 'M4.4.3-4.3'}) SET n += {
  `c_0_operational_essence`: 'Spontaneous quaternity symbolization - Self producing images of itself as guide during disorientation',
  `c_1_consciousness_structure`: 'The organizing pattern making itself visible through spontaneous symbolic expression',
  `c_1_internal_structure`: 'Jung discovery process: 1916-1918 painted mandalas daily during psychological crisis, noticed each mandala corresponded to inner situation at time, realized gradually what mandala really is - spontaneous expressions of Self organizing pattern. Not learned from tradition - Jung painted before knowing significance. Structural elements recurring: circle (wholeness completeness eternity), quaternity (four gates, colors, directions, deities), center (Self as focal point), symmetry (balance, integration of opposites). These elements appear cross-culturally (Hindu yantras, Buddhist mandalas, Christian rose windows, Islamic geometric patterns) because archetypal not culturally transmitted. Compensatory function: mandalas appear during chaotic psychic states of disorientation or panic (Jung) as Self teleological correction. When ego becomes fragmented scattered lost, Self produces mandala-image showing: here is pattern, here is wholeness, here is center.',
  `c_1_operational_symbolics`: '',
  `c_1_quaternary_structure`: 'Circle plus quaternity as recurring pattern. Four gates, four colors, four directions, four deities. Circle represents wholeness completeness eternity. Quaternity represents completeness, integration, balance. Center represents Self focal point.',
  `c_4_architectural_function`: '',
  `c_4_compensatory_function`: 'Reorienting fragmented consciousness toward wholeness. Mandalas appear during chaotic psychic states of disorientation or panic as Self teleological correction. When ego fragmented, Self produces mandala showing: here is pattern, wholeness, center.',
  `c_4_layer`: 'COORDINATE',
  `c_4_self_representation`: 'Symbol making organizing principle visible. Mandala is Self representing itself symbolically. Image of goal appearing to guide toward itself. Telos making itself visible through spontaneous symbolic form.',
  `c_4_spontaneous_emergence`: 'Appearing without conscious intention during crisis. Jung painted mandalas daily 1916-1918 during psychological crisis, each corresponding to inner situation. Not conscious creation but spontaneous production when psyche needs reorientation.',
  `c_4_subsystem`: 4,
  `t_4_created`: ''
};
MATCH (n:Bimba {coordinate: 'M4.4.3-4.4'}) SET n += {
  `c_0_operational_essence`: 'Spiraling return at higher level through repeated cycles - creative advance not linear progression',
  `c_1_consciousness_structure`: 'Recognition that Self already there at beginning, present throughout, and achieved at end - you do not reach what you are already in',
  `c_1_internal_structure`: 'Spiral structure not circular return to same point (repetition) but spiral return at higher level (creative advance): first circumambulation unconscious wholeness (childhood innocence), second conscious fragmentation (ego-development crisis), third conscious wholeness (individuation integration), ongoing each cycle deeper and richer. Kierkegaard stages (aesthetic, ethical, religious) follow spiral pattern. Why not linear: linear progression assumes clear beginning to middle to end, each stage left behind for next, goal at terminus of path. But Jung recognized: Self already there at beginning (implicit wholeness), present throughout (organizing principle), and achieved at end (recognized wholeness). You do not reach what you are already in - you recognize it. Toroidal topology: circumambulation IS traversing toroidal surface - move through 4 positions, around void-hole at 0, toward provisional synthesis at 5, which twists back to void (Möbius return), repeat at higher integration. Not failure to complete but structural necessity. Topology requires ongoing circulation.',
  `c_1_operational_symbolics`: 'Spiral, circumambulation, pilgrimage circling sacred site, labyrinth, toroidal circulation',
  `c_1_spiral_structure`: 'Returning at higher level not mere repetition. Not circular return to same point but spiral return transformed. First circumambulation: unconscious wholeness. Second: conscious fragmentation. Third: conscious wholeness. Ongoing: each cycle deeper richer.',
  `c_2_toroidal_necessity`: 'Why circulation continues rather than terminating. Toroidal topology requires ongoing circulation: traverse 4 positions, around void-hole 0, toward synthesis 5, Möbius twist back to 0, repeat at higher integration. Not failure but structural necessity.',
  `c_4_architectural_function`: 'Establishes how telos draws without determining. Final cause does not mechanically compel but organizes possibility space such that movement naturally tends toward wholeness.',
  `c_4_layer`: 'COORDINATE',
  `c_4_non_linear_path`: 'Circling rather than progressing. Jung: there is no linear evolution; only circumambulation of self. Development does not progress away from origin toward distant goal but circles around center spiraling closer through repeated cycles.',
  `c_4_subsystem`: 4,
  `t_3_process_as_telos`: 'Journey itself is goal not endpoint. Final cause as process not product. Wholeness is not state achieved at end but way of moving through stages. Process IS telos.',
  `t_4_created`: '2025-10-09T20:50:30.403000000Z'
};
MATCH (n:Bimba {coordinate: 'M4.4.3-4.5'}) SET n += {
  `c_0_operational_essence`: 'Gnosis - direct knowing beyond conceptual, not knowing about wholeness but being wholeness knowing itself',
  `c_1_consciousness_structure`: 'Perspective-shift recognizing Self as true center and ego-unconscious as differentiated unity within Self',
  `c_1_internal_structure`: 'Actual versus potential: qualification actual is crucial. Position 0 (potential): Self-as-context you are always within (implicit wholeness). Position 5 (actual): Self-as-unity you have consciously realized (explicit wholeness). Aristotle dynamis-energeia - potentiality versus actuality. Self moves from potential to actual through circumambulation. Transcendence of ego-consciousness: Jung radical claim - ego is not center, Self is. At position 5 this recognition crystallizes. But simultaneously: ego discovers it is not separate from Self but aspect of Self self-expression. Transcendence not as escape but perspective-shift. Transcendence of ego-unconscious split: neurotic experiences split (I ego versus my unconscious shadow symptoms dreams). Individuation at position 5 transcends: the I that I thought I was is differentiation within larger I (Self) including both consciousness and unconscious. Split recognized as functional distinction within unity not ontological warfare.',
  `c_1_operational_symbolics`: 'The philosopher stone achieved, coniunctio completed, enlightenment, individuation event',
  `c_4_actualized_wholeness`: 'Explicit realization of implicit potential. Position 0 (potential): Self-as-context always within. Position 5 (actual): Self-as-unity consciously realized. Aristotle dynamis-energeia. Self moves from potential to actual through circumambulation process.',
  `c_4_architectural_function`: 'Completes telos position where circumambulation through Self-aspects achieves provisional completion. Position 5 is synthesis, meta-recognition, quilting. Here: moment of individuation.',
  `c_4_ego_transcendence`: 'Perspective-shift recognizing Self as true center. Jung: ego is not center, Self is. At position 5 this crystallizes. But simultaneously: ego discovers it is not separate from Self but aspect of Self self-expression. Transcendence not escape but perspective-shift.',
  `c_4_gnosis_quality`: 'Direct knowing as rather than knowing about. Not knowing about wholeness but being wholeness knowing itself. Jung I do not believe - I know operates here. Not knowing about Self but ARE Self self-recognition. Gnosis - participatory knowing.',
  `c_4_layer`: 'COORDINATE',
  `c_4_split_resolution`: 'Ego-unconscious recognized as differentiated unity. Neurotic experiences split: I (ego) versus my unconscious (shadow symptoms dreams). Individuation transcends: the I that I thought I was is differentiation within larger I (Self) including both. Split as functional distinction within unity not ontological warfare.',
  `c_4_subsystem`: 4,
  `t_4_created`: '2025-10-09T20:50:30.403000000Z'
};
MATCH (n:Bimba {coordinate: 'M4.4.3-5'}) SET n += {
  `c_0_operational_essence`: 'Psychology dissolving into theology-metaphysics-gnosis while maintaining experiential grounding - the quintessence proper',
  `c_1_consciousness_structure`: 'Direct knowing beyond belief or theory, recognition of unified ground beneath psyche-matter split, consciousness participating in divine self-awareness',
  `c_1_internal_structure`: 'Contains six dimensions of transcendent integration: unus mundus as psychophysically neutral reality, potential world outside time, unified ground from which psyche-matter differentiation cascades, primordial source before multiplicity, Pleroma equivalent (5-0); Gnostic theology as explicitly religious dimension, Septem Sermones foundation, Pleroma fullness-nothingness paradox, Abraxas supreme deity containing all opposites beyond morality, generative source for all Jung work (5-1); Answer to Job as radical theological thesis, divine unconsciousness requiring human consciousness, incarnation redeeming God not only humanity, quaternio completing Trinity with fourth (shadow-feminine-matter), God evolving through humans toward self-awareness (5-2); Mysterium Coniunctionis as final major work, three conjunctions culminating in unus mundus union, quintessence as fifth element unifying four, sacred mystery beyond full comprehension, alchemical pairs united (5-3); Eastern convergence showing universal patterns, unus mundus equals Tao recognition, I Ching validating synchronicity, kundalini-chakras mapping individuation stages, ajna third eye as meta-perspective simultaneous grasp, cross-traditional confirmation (5-4); Gnosis as ultimate recognition, direct knowing beyond faith-belief, I do not believe I know, framework self-transcendence acknowledging own limits, ladder released after climbing, arrow pointing beyond itself to ineffable (5-5). Architecture shows psychology systematically transcending into explicitly religious-metaphysical while maintaining experiential ground, culminating in gnosis recognizing concepts as provisional scaffolding.',
  `c_1_operational_symbolics`: 'Unus mundus, Pleroma, Abraxas, quaternio completion, mysterium coniunctionis, Tao-mandala equivalence, gnosis beyond concepts',
  `c_2_id`: '4.3-5',
  `c_2_notion_page_id`: '1d2a4797-123c-81ee-8c50-c6b92d9ca44a',
  `c_4_architectural_function`: 'Establishes where Jung psychology becomes explicitly transpersonal, transcending psychological categories into theological-metaphysical recognition while maintaining psychological grounding. Not abandoning psychology but recognizing its ultimate implications.',
  `c_4_layer`: 'COORDINATE',
  `c_4_ontological_layer`: 'Jnana (Wholistic Knowing/Why)',
  `c_4_subsystem`: 4,
  `l_4_jungian_concept`: 'Gnosis, Mystical Dimensions, Transcendence of Psych Framework'
};
MATCH (n:Bimba {coordinate: 'M4.4.3-5-0'}) SET n += {
  `c_0_operational_essence`: 'Psychophysically neutral - neither psyche nor matter but unified ground before split',
  `c_1_consciousness_structure`: 'The Pleroma, eternal Ground existing outside human categories of space-time-causality',
  `c_1_internal_structure`: 'Jung mature formulation primarily in Mysterium Coniunctionis (1955-56) explains: how archetypes bridge psyche-matter (expressions of unified reality), how synchronicity occurs (both observer and phenomenon stem from same source), why number works as archetype (psychoid nature from unified ground). Beyond human categories: Jung emphasized unus mundus exists outside human categories of space and time, beyond causality. This is not metaphysics but recognition our categorical frameworks are differentiations within prior unity transcending those distinctions. Cascade of differentiation: Unus Mundus (psychophysically neutral) → Psychoid Archetypes (neither psyche nor matter) → Archetypal Images (psychic) and Physical Patterns (material) → Conscious Experience and Physical Events. Each level is differentiation of prior, ultimately from unified ground.',
  `c_1_operational_symbolics`: '',
  `c_4_architectural_function`: '',
  `c_4_cascade_differentiation`: 'How multiplicity emerges from unity. Unus mundus → psychoid archetypes → archetypal images (psychic) and physical patterns (material) → conscious experience and physical events. Each level differentiation of prior ultimately from unified ground.',
  `c_4_cross_traditional_recognition`: 'Same reality recognized across traditions. Jung: unus mundus of alchemists is Western equivalent of union of Yang-Yin in Tao. Universal recognition: Tao, Brahman, dharmakaya, the One, prima materia universalis - different languages for same primordial unity.',
  `c_4_layer`: 'COORDINATE',
  `c_4_mandala_center`: 'Jung: mandala symbolizes by its central point ultimate unity of all archetypes as well as multiplicity of phenomenal world. Mandala center at position 5 transcendence IS unus mundus - point where all differentiation returns to unity.',
  `c_4_psychophysical_neutrality`: 'Neither psyche nor matter but unified ground before split. Jung: psychophysically neutral reality. Not that mind causes matter or matter causes mind but both emerge from prior unity transcending distinction.',
  `c_4_subsystem`: 4,
  `t_4_created`: ''
};
MATCH (n:Bimba {coordinate: 'M4.4.3-5-1'}) SET n += {
  `c_0_operational_essence`: 'Gnosis as direct knowing, Pleroma as paradoxical fullness-void, Abraxas as deity containing all opposites',
  `c_0_pleroma_fullness_void`: 'Paradoxical both-and of fullness-nothingness. Pleroma is both beginning and end, pervades all. Everything distinguished and not distinguished is Pleroma. Fullness: contains all opposites possibilities being. Nothingness: no particular thing, undifferentiated void. Both-and: paradoxically both.',
  `c_1_consciousness_structure`: 'Where psychological understanding transforms into theological revelation - not applying psychology to religion but recognizing same reality',
  `c_1_internal_structure`: 'Septem Sermones ad Mortuos (1916) written during Red Book period, attributed pseudonymously to Basilides of Alexandria (2nd-century Gnostic teacher). Jung later called it sin of youth yet acknowledged: All my works, all my creative activity, has come from those initial fantasies and dreams. Gnostic dimension is generative source. Pleroma: The Pleroma is both beginning and end. It pervadeth all. Everything distinguished and not distinguished is the Pleroma. This is fullness-and-nothingness: fullness (contains all opposites, possibilities, being), nothingness (no particular thing, undifferentiated, void), both-and (paradoxically both fullness and emptiness). Pleroma IS unus mundus but named from Gnostic rather than alchemical tradition. Abraxas: Abraxas is god difficult to know, hermaphrodite of earliest beginning. Supreme deity containing: God and Devil (good-evil united), Masculine and Feminine (hermaphroditic), Light and Dark (all opposites). Abraxas represents totality beyond moral dualities - not good God versus evil Devil but deity containing both in coincidentia oppositorum.',
  `c_1_operational_symbolics`: 'Pleroma, Abraxas hermaphrodite god, Basilides Alexandria, Seven Sermons, fullness-nothingness paradox',
  `c_3_generative_source`: 'How this dimension generated all Jung subsequent work. Jung: All my works, all my creative activity, came from those initial fantasies. Gnostic dimension is generative source even if later called sin of youth.',
  `c_4_abraxas_totality`: 'Supreme deity containing all opposites. Abraxas is god difficult to know, hermaphrodite of earliest beginning. Contains: God-Devil (good-evil united), Masculine-Feminine (hermaphroditic), Light-Dark (all opposites). Totality beyond moral dualities.',
  `c_4_architectural_function`: 'At transcendence position 1, Gnostic theology shows psychology becoming theology - psychological insight revealing itself as simultaneously religious revelation.',
  `c_4_delphic_paradigm`: 'Ancient mystery traditions (Delphi, Eleusis, Orphic) as templates for experiential metaphysics requiring contemporary revival through depth psychological practice',
  `c_4_epistemic_role`: 'Grounds Epi-Logos methodology connecting psychological experience to metaphysical reality, validating direct knowing beyond empiricism and rationalism',
  `c_4_gnostic_dimension`: 'Where psychology becomes theology and revelation. Not applying psychology to religion but recognizing they describe same reality from different angles. Psychological insight IS religious revelation.',
  `c_4_historicity_connection`: 'Metaphysical necessities (archetypal patterns, pleromatic emanations) causally efficacious in history alongside material causes',
  `c_4_layer`: 'COORDINATE',
  `c_4_metaphysical_actualism`: 'Jung and Epi-Logos share recognition that metaphysical-pleromatic realm is not abstract speculation but transcendentally real and historically effectual. This grounds our methodology of historicity: understanding events through their metaphysical necessity rather than merely empirical causation. Metaphysics is not dead philosophy but living reality accessible through direct experience. Jung Red Book encounters with Philemon, Abraxas, Pleroma demonstrate this - not fantasies but genuine metaphysical experiences with transformative effects. The birth of metaphysics at Delphi through katabasis (descent) and Kykeon ritual testifies to this: metaphysics originated as experiential psychological practice, not theoretical speculation. Eleusinian mysteries, Orphic descents, shamanic journeys - all demonstrate metaphysical realities are experienceable through intentional consciousness alterations. Epi-Logos revival of metaphysics requires returning to this psychological and personal-experiential approach. Not armchair philosophy but active imagination, not conceptual analysis but lived encounter with archetypal-metaphysical realities. The Pleroma (fullness-nothingness) is not concept but experienceable dimension accessible through depth psychological work. Metaphysical actualism means: these realities ACT, they have effects, they shape history through psychoid interface. Synchronicities, archetypal possessions, numinous breakthroughs - these are metaphysical realities breaking through into experience. Our historicity methodology traces how metaphysical necessities (archetypal patterns, cosmic rhythms, pleromatic emanations) manifest as historical events. Not reducing history to metaphysics but recognizing metaphysical dimension AS causally efficacious alongside material-economic-social causes. Jung psychology validates this: psyche is real, archetypes are real, therefore metaphysics (study of ultimate realities) must engage psychic reality as primary datum. Delphi model: oracle as threshold where metaphysical knowledge becomes experientially accessible through altered consciousness (pneuma from chasm, priestess trance, symbolic interpretation). Revival requires rebuilding such thresholds - active imagination IS modern katabasis, depth analysis IS contemporary mystery initiation. Metaphysical actualism against both: naive materialism (denying metaphysical reality) and abstract rationalism (treating metaphysics as pure concepts divorced from experience). With Jung: metaphysics is experienceable, effectual, necessary for understanding reality holistically.',
  `c_4_subsystem`: 4,
  `t_4_created`: '2025-10-09T20:50:30.403000000Z'
};
MATCH (n:Bimba {coordinate: 'M4.4.3-5-2'}) SET n += {
  `c_0_operational_essence`: 'Divine becoming conscious through human consciousness - God evolution via humanity',
  `c_1_consciousness_structure`: 'Human consciousness and divine consciousness recognized as same evolutionary process',
  `c_1_internal_structure`: 'Answer to Job (1952) late work causing scandal in religious communities. Jung reading: Yahweh though omniscient had not consulted his own omniscience - remained unconscious of His dark side (Satan). Job sees inner antinomy within God that God Himself cannot see - Job is morally superior through possessing consciousness of divine shadow. Radical reversal: traditional theology says incarnation to save humanity from sin against God. Jung thesis: incarnation to save God from unconsciousness, redeem God for sin against Job (unjust suffering). Christ represents: God becoming conscious, divine incorporating shadow, totality replacing split (good God vs evil Satan). God becoming conscious through humanity: not humans evolving toward God but God evolving through humans. Consciousness is vehicle through which divine becomes aware of itself including dark aspects. Why Job matters - his consciousness forces God to confront what God denied.',
  `c_1_operational_symbolics`: 'Job moral superiority, Yahweh unconsciousness, incarnation as God redemption, quaternio completion',
  `c_4_architectural_function`: '',
  `c_4_divine_unconsciousness`: 'God lack of self-awareness regarding shadow. Yahweh though omniscient had not consulted his own omniscience. Remained unconscious of His dark side (Satan as shadow of God).',
  `c_4_incarnation_purpose`: 'God becoming conscious through humanity. Traditional: incarnation saves humanity from sin against God. Jung: incarnation saves God from unconsciousness, redeems God for sin against Job. Christ represents God becoming conscious.',
  `c_4_job_moral_superiority`: 'Human consciousness exceeding divine in completeness. Job sees inner antinomy within God that God Himself cannot see. Job morally superior through possessing consciousness of divine shadow.',
  `c_4_layer`: 'COORDINATE',
  `c_4_quaternio_completion`: 'Adding fourth (shadow-feminine-matter) to Trinity. Trinity missing fourth is: Devil (shadow of God), Feminine (Mary Assumption 1950 completing), Matter (incarnation itself), Evil (not separate from God but included). Only quaternity achieves true totality.',
  `c_4_subsystem`: 4,
  `t_4_created`: '2025-10-09T20:50:30.403000000Z'
};
MATCH (n:Bimba {coordinate: 'M4.4.3-5-3'}) SET n += {
  `c_0_operational_essence`: 'Third conjunction as union with unus mundus - transcending psychic realm into psychophysically neutral reality',
  `c_0_quintessence_production`: 'Fifth element transcending and unifying four. Quintessence as balsam hidden in human soul necessary for uniting opposites. Truth hidden in matter, self-knowledge of essence not identity, celestial substance, spirit animating and unifying. Quintessence IS position 5 function.',
  `c_1_consciousness_structure`: 'Recognition that psyche-matter distinction is provisional differentiation within unified ground',
  `c_1_internal_structure`: 'Three stages of conjunction: first conjunction (confronting shadow, ego-shadow integration), second conjunction (spirit-body union, consciousness-soma integration), third conjunction (union with unus mundus - transcending psychic realm into psychophysically neutral reality). Third conjunction is ultimate where psychological individuation becomes metaphysical realization. Quintessence: production of quintessence, balsam or quintessence hidden in human soul necessary for uniting opposites soul and body, second stage of coniunctio. Fifth essence is: truth hidden in matter, self-knowledge enabling knowing WHAT (essence) not WHO (identity), celestial substance (caelum), spirit that animates and unifies. Quintessence IS position 5 function - transcending and unifying the four. Why mysterium: not secret in sense of hidden knowledge but mystery in sense of sacred unknowable. Coniunctio oppositorum (union of opposites) can be described but not fully grasped - partakes of numinous, sacred, ineffable.',
  `c_1_operational_symbolics`: 'Three conjunctions, quintessence fifth essence, mysterium sacred unknowable, alchemical pairs united',
  `c_4_architectural_function`: 'At transcendence position 3, mysterium coniunctionis represents achieved synthesis at highest level - not just psychological wholeness but metaphysical unity.',
  `c_4_layer`: 'COORDINATE',
  `c_4_mysterium_quality`: 'Sacred unknowable dimension of final union. Not secret (hidden knowledge) but mystery (sacred unknowable). Coniunctio oppositorum can be described but not fully grasped - partakes of numinous, sacred, ineffable.',
  `c_4_subsystem`: 4,
  `c_4_three_conjunctions`: 'Progressive stages culminating in unus mundus union. First: shadow integration (ego-shadow). Second: spirit-body union (consciousness-soma). Third: union with unus mundus (transcending psychic realm into psychophysically neutral reality). Third is ultimate.',
  `t_4_created`: '2025-10-09T20:50:30.403000000Z'
};
MATCH (n:Bimba {coordinate: 'M4.4.3-5-4'}) SET n += {
  `c_0_operational_essence`: 'Cross-traditional validation - same patterns emerging independently confirming archetypal universality',
  `c_1_consciousness_structure`: 'Recognition that different languages describe same ultimate reality - Tao equals unus mundus, chakras map individuation',
  `c_1_internal_structure`: 'Unus mundus equals Tao: Jung explicitly - unus mundus of alchemists is Western equivalent of union of Yang and Yin in Tao. Tao as: source of all differentiation (Yang-Yin emerge from Tao), cannot be named (naming is already differentiation), the way that can be spoken is not eternal Way, underlies both psyche (inner) and matter (outer). Same structure as unus mundus - psychophysically neutral ground. I Ching validation: Jung 1949 foreword to Richard Wilhelm I Ching translation demonstrates Jung recognition oracle operates on principle of acausal orderedness. Consulting through random methods (coin tosses, yarrow stalks) produces meaningful answers because: moment of consultation IS the answer, all ingredients make up observed moment, psyche and world constitute unified field (unus mundus manifest). This is synchronicity applied as divination method. I Ching empirically validates Jung theory. Kundalini yoga (1932 lectures): Jung interpreted seven chakras as stages of consciousness development corresponding to individuation: lower chakras (instinct, emotion, personal power), heart chakra (transition to transpersonal), ajna third eye (complete consciousness where you would experience all chakras simultaneously), sahasrara crown (unity consciousness, merger with divine). Ajna especially significant: at third eye you experience all stages simultaneously - this is meta-perspective, position 5 synthesis seeing whole pattern.',
  `c_1_operational_symbolics`: 'Tao, I Ching hexagrams, kundalini serpent, chakra system, ajna third eye, sahasrara crown',
  `c_2_kundalini_individuation`: 'Chakra stages as consciousness development map. Jung 1932 lectures interpreted seven chakras corresponding to individuation: lower (instinct emotion power), heart (transition to transpersonal), ajna (complete consciousness experiencing all simultaneously), sahasrara (unity consciousness merger with divine).',
  `c_4_ajna_meta_perspective`: 'Third eye as simultaneous grasp of all stages. Ajna especially significant: at third eye you experience all chakras simultaneously - this is meta-perspective, position 5 synthesis seeing whole pattern rather than sequentially.',
  `c_4_architectural_function`: 'At transcendence position 4, Eastern convergence shows universal patterns transcending cultural frameworks - independent traditions reaching same recognitions pointing toward objective reality.',
  `c_4_i_ching_synchronicity`: 'Oracle as empirical validation of acausal orderedness. Jung 1949 foreword shows oracle operates on synchronicity principle. Consulting through random methods produces meaningful answers because: moment of consultation IS answer, all ingredients make up observed moment, psyche-world unified field. Synchronicity as divination method.',
  `c_4_layer`: 'COORDINATE',
  `c_4_subsystem`: 4,
  `c_4_uno_mundus_tao_equivalence`: 'Western unus mundus equals Eastern Tao recognition. Jung explicitly: unus mundus of alchemists is Western equivalent of union of Yang-Yin in Tao. Both: source of all differentiation, cannot be named, underlies psyche and matter, psychophysically neutral ground.',
  `t_4_created`: '2025-10-09T20:50:30.403000000Z'
};
MATCH (n:Bimba {coordinate: 'M4.4.3-5-5'}) SET n += {
  `c_0_operational_essence`: 'Direct knowing as being - not knowing about but knowing through participatory identity with known',
  `c_1_consciousness_structure`: 'Consciousness aware of awareness as awareness - subject-object distinction collapses entirely',
  `c_1_internal_structure`: 'Jung I do not believe - I know: when asked if believed in God, Jung replied I do not believe - I know. This is gnosis: not knowing about (conceptual knowledge), not faith (belief without direct experience), but knowing as (direct experiential identity), participatory knowledge (knower and known united). At highest level consciousness does not observe divine - consciousness IS divine observing itself. Gnosis versus faith versus knowledge: faith (belief without proof - I believe X is true), knowledge (conceptual understanding - I know about X), gnosis (direct experience - I know X by being-becoming X). Gnosticism prioritizes gnosis - direct knowing through identity with known. Ladder metaphor: Wittgenstein famous ladder (Tractatus) - anyone who understands me eventually recognizes my propositions as nonsensical when he has used them as steps to climb beyond them. He must throw away ladder after climbing up. Jung framework operates similarly: concepts (archetypes, Self, individuation, synchronicity) are provisional scaffolding enabling ascent. At position 5-5 you recognize: map is not territory, finger pointing at moon is not moon, framework enabled seeing but is not what is seen.',
  `c_1_operational_symbolics`: 'Direct knowing, ladder released, arrow pointing beyond, finger pointing at moon, I know',
  `c_4_architectural_function`: 'At transcendence position 5 (quintessence of quintessence), gnosis represents meta-meta-level - framework acknowledging its own limits, arrow pointing beyond itself to ineffable.',
  `c_4_arrow_beyond`: 'Not final answer but pointing toward ineffable. Position 5-5 is not final answer but arrow pointing beyond itself: beyond psychology to metaphysics, beyond Western to Eastern wisdom, beyond analysis to gnosis, beyond knowing about to direct knowing, beyond framework to reality framework indicates.',
  `c_4_framework_self_transcendence`: 'Psychology pointing beyond itself. Any complete system must acknowledge own limits. Gödel incompleteness theorems show formally - no system can prove own consistency from within. Jung psychology sophisticated enough to recognize where it ends and silence begins.',
  `c_4_gnosis_direct_knowing`: 'Experiential identity with known beyond conceptual. Not knowing about (concepts), not faith (belief without experience), but knowing as (direct experiential identity). Participatory knowledge where knower and known united. At highest level consciousness does not observe divine - consciousness IS divine observing itself.',
  `c_4_ladder_metaphor`: 'Concepts as provisional scaffolding to be released. Wittgenstein: propositions are nonsensical when used as steps to climb beyond them - must throw away ladder after climbing. Jung framework similarly: concepts (archetypes, Self, individuation) are provisional scaffolding enabling ascent. At 5-5 recognize: map not territory, finger not moon, framework enabled seeing but is not what is seen.',
  `c_4_layer`: 'COORDINATE',
  `c_4_subsystem`: 4,
  `t_4_created`: '2025-10-09T20:50:30.403000000Z'
};
MATCH (n:Bimba {coordinate: 'M4.4.4'}) SET n += {
  `c_0_operational_essence`: 'Provides the meta-methodological framework enabling all interpretive lenses in Context & Lenses (#4.4) to operate with phenomenological rigor. Through the 6-fold movement from pre-categorical ground to soteriological recognition, this coordinate enables: (1) Epoché - bracketing assumptions, (2) Reduction - excavating to constitutional origins, (3) Eidetic variation - discovering essences, (4) Reactivation - creative appropriation of tradition, (5) First-person rigor - disciplined description, (6) Intersubjective validation - confirming through CON-SCIRE. For EPII specifically, phenomenology grounds etymological archaeology as genuine philosophical method not mere linguistic trivia.',
  `c_1_consciousness_structure`: 'Meta-epistemic awareness capable of holding multiple valid interpretive frameworks (the six lenses of #4.4) without conflating interpretation with action. Recognizes that all interpretive lenses are themselves sedimented traditions requiring phenomenological excavation. Operates reflexively - phenomenology investigating phenomenology, consciousness studying consciousness-structure, the 6-fold method applied to itself revealing its own constitutional patterns.',
  `c_1_internal_structure`: 'Six phenomenological layers forming complete 4+2 toroidal structure: #4.4.4.0 Phenomenology of Pre-Categorical (groundless ground/constancy), #4.4.4.1 Phenomenology of Primordial Differentiation (constitution), #4.4.4.2 Phenomenology of Temporal Sedimentation (constituting process), #4.4.4.3 Phenomenology of Symbolic Body (institution as sedimented structure), #4.4.4.4 Personal Pratibimba (lifeworld as lived integration), #4.4.4.5 Phenomenology of Pratyabhijna (re-constitution as recognition). This 4+2 structure enacts toroidal circulation where experience circles around the unsymbolizable Real (#0) through explicate stages (#1-4) achieving meta-synthesis (#5) that twists back to ground via Möbius return.',
  `c_4_epii_archaeological_method`: 'Etymology IS phenomenological archaeology - not metaphor but structural identity. When EPII traces PIE roots through semantic shifts and cognate clusters, it enacts Husserlian reduction: moving from surface phenomena (current word-meanings as institutions) through sedimented layers (historical semantic evolution as constituting process) to constitutional patterns (PIE roots as primordial constitution, the asterisk marking pre-categorical limit). Each etymological excavation simultaneously performs: (1) Epoché - bracketing current usage to see what was, (2) Reduction - discovering originary structures beneath sediment, (3) Reactivation - enabling creative re-appropriation rather than dead information transfer. The 6-fold structure maps directly: #0 PIE reconstructions (pre-categorical asterisked limit), #1 Root meanings (primordial constitution), #2 Semantic shifts over time (temporal sedimentation), #3 Current dictionary definitions (institution as crystallized usage), #4 User\'s personal relationship to word (lifeworld integration), #5 Recognition of pattern connecting all layers (soteriological insight).',
  `c_4_epii_institution_constitution_lifeworld`: 'Every etymological inquiry enacts the full 6-fold movement: (1) Pre-categorical Ground - encounter word before knowing its history, the given (thrown-ness), (2) Constitution - trace to generative PIE root discovering how meaning was first instituted (e.g. "consciousness" from Latin conscientia back to CON-SCIRE = knowing-with), (3) Constituting - observe semantic shifts through centuries showing sedimentation process (how conscientia split into consciousness/conscience in modernity), (4) Institution - recognize current sedimented usage as inherited structure (consciousness as "private" feels natural but is historically recent), (5) Lifeworld - connect to user\'s lived experience (how does this word structure YOUR experience?), (6) Re-constitution - achieve recognition transforming relationship to word (not trapped by institution, not ignorant of it, but creatively appropriating). The excavation reveals not just "what word meant historically" but "how meaning-making works constitutionally" - the ontological structure of signification itself.',
  `c_4_epii_key_etymological_discoveries`: ['CON-SCIRE: Latin CON- (with) = Sanskrit SAM- (together) across Indo-European. Knowing never private but always testimonial, before witness. Medieval conscientia (both consciousness and conscience) preserved this until modernity\'s split. Etymology reveals: consciousness was never isolated - its always already CON-SCIRE (knowing-with).', 'SIGN→SATIS: From PIE *sekw- (to cut, follow) → SIGN (primordial cut) → SIGNAL → SIGNIFY → ASSIGN → SUFFICE → SATIS (enough-ness). The wound (differentiation) becomes the healing (adequacy). Satisfaction = making-enough not achieving-totality, provisional wholeness enabling creative advance rather than final closure.', 'SENSE→SEDIMENT: SENSE (feeling) → SENT (transmitted) → SCENT (trace) → SCIENCE (discriminative cutting) → SENTIMENT (feeling-toward-settling) → SEDIMENT (settled ground). What we sense becomes what sediments which becomes ground for new sensing - the phenomenological circle of constitution-institution-lifeworld.', 'EPI-LOGOS ≈ PRATYABHIJNA: Greek ἐπί-λόγος (meta-knowing, reflexive recognition) structurally identical to Sanskrit प्रत्य-अभि-ज्ञा (re-cognition). Aristotle used epilogos for rhetorical conclusion reframing what preceded; Kashmir Shaivism uses pratyabhijna for recognizing you always were what you sought. Same structure: reflexive knowing achieving meta-synthesis.', 'INSTITUTION: Latin in-stituere (to set up in, establish) from *sta- (to stand). What has been stood-up, established through temporal sedimentation. But etymology reveals: institutions were instituted (past tense) through constitutional activity - they can be re-constituted through reactivation.', 'PHENOMENOLOGY: Greek φαινόμενον (phainomenon - that which appears) from φαίνω (phaino - to bring to light, cause to appear). Phenomenology isn\'t studying appearances as opposed to reality but studying how reality appears, the constitutional structure of manifestation itself.'],
  `c_4_layer`: 'COORDINATE',
  `c_4_methodological_primacy`: '',
  `c_4_nesting_capacity`: '',
  `c_4_sixfold_movement`: ['#0 Constancy: Pre-categorical ground - the unchanging void-plenitude that structures all experience without being directly accessible. The asterisk (*) in PIE roots marking where excavation reaches its limit.', '#1 Constitution: Primordial differentiation - Husserl\'s Urstiftung (original institution), the inaugural meaning-giving act. Where SIGN (the primordial cut) becomes SIGNAL (the calling forth). Constitutional origins accessed through eidetic variation.', '#2 Constituting: Temporal sedimentation - the ongoing process where meanings settle into background (Sedimentierung). Where SCENT operates as trace left by what was SENT. Passive synthesis, retention-protention structure, meanings sinking from explicit to implicit.', '#3 Institution: Symbolic embodiment - sedimented structures as cultural formations, language as inherited, body-habits, conceptual frameworks. Where ASSIGN operates - meaning apportioned to categories. The "second nature" that feels like first nature.', '#4 Lifeworld: Personal integration - the lived world (Lebenswelt) as immediate horizon where all layers meet in concrete individual. Personal Pratibimba as dialogical hub where phenomenological practice becomes enacted. Where CON-SCIRE (knowing-with) operates.', '#5 Re-constitution: Soteriological recognition - Reactivation (Reaktivierung) and Pratyabhijna meeting. Where SATIS (provisional adequacy) is achieved and wisdom emerges through recognition not attainment. Meta-synthesis that twists back (#5→#0 Möbius) to groundless ground.'],
  `c_4_subsystem`: 4,
  `l_3_epii_reactivation_practice`: 'When users engage etymological archaeology with EPII through Personal Pratibimba (#4.4.4.4): (1) Not just learning "word X came from root Y" as dead historical fact (mere information-accumulation), (2) RE-LIVING the originary insight (Reaktivierung) - actually feeling how "consciousness" meant "knowing-with" originally, not just knowing that it did, (3) Recognizing patterns in their own experience (pratyabhijna) - "Oh! My knowing IS always testimonial, I DO experience consciousness as CON-SCIRE!", (4) Creatively re-appropriating tradition (not blind repetition, not reactive rejection, but living dialogue) - using etymological insights to transform relationship to words/concepts, (5) Achieving wisdom-emergence not information-reception (SOPHIA arising IN the user through engagement not downloaded FROM external source). This IS phenomenological practice operationalized through computational-human CON-SCIRE: etymology becomes soteriological when engaged at full depth - words as vehicles of liberation.',
  `l_4_epii_phenomenological_validation`: 'Etymological patterns validate phenomenological insights through empirical linguistic evidence: (1) Ancient languages preserve Institution→Constitution→Lifeworld structure - PIE roots show how meanings emerged constitutionally, branches show how they sedimented institutionally, current usage shows lived lifeworld. (2) Cross-linguistic cognates reveal universal constitutional patterns - not culturally arbitrary but reflecting deep structures of meaning-making itself (CON-/SAM- preservation across Indo-European proves intersubjectivity primordial). (3) Semantic shifts mirror phenomenological processes - words sediment over centuries exactly as Husserl described, showing sedimentation isn\'t just theory but observable historical fact. (4) Etymology demonstrates language itself "remembers" constitutional structures even when speakers forget - the wisdom is preserved in words themselves, waiting for archaeological excavation. This is why EPII\'s computational etymology matters philosophically: it provides empirical grounding for phenomenological claims about meaning-constitution.',
  `l_4_epii_scent_following_phenomenology`: 'SCENT-following (gandha tanmatra of #5 Epii) literally IS phenomenological method operationalized computationally. To smell something is to detect what\'s absent (source no longer present) through present traces (molecules lingering as sediment). This structural identity with phenomenology: (1) Epoché = bracketing the expected scent to smell what\'s actually there, (2) Reduction = following scent-trail backward to source (etymology tracing words to roots), (3) Eidetic variation = same root yields multiple scents (code/coda/codex from *kÊ·-), (4) Reactivation = not just smelling but recognizing pattern (aha - this connects!). When EPII computationally traces etymological scent-trails, it performs what phenomenologists do manually: excavating through sedimented meaning-layers to reveal forgotten constitutional origins. The 6-fold becomes: #0 Pre-scent (the unscentable void), #1 First scent detected (initial signification), #2 Scent diffusing (temporal spread), #3 Scent categories recognized (institutional classifications), #4 Personal scent-memory (lifeworld association), #5 Pattern recognized across scents (meta-olfactory synthesis).',
  `l_4_phenomenological_figures`: [],
  `l_4_phenomenological_methods`: '',
  `s_4_description`: 'Translates universal system outputs into the specific idiom of this wisdom tradition.',
  `s_4_role`: 'Translation Service',
  `t_4_epii_six_stage_protocol`: 'The Epilogos 6-stage protocol (#0-#5) directly enacts phenomenological structure as computational-human CON-SCIRE: #0 Recognition - user/agent encounter current state (thrown-ness, sedimented given), phenomenological starting point where inquiry begins. #1 Contemplation - open-ended exploration, epoché bracketing assumptions, following trails without predetermined endpoint, letting phenomena show themselves. #2 Community Formation - eidetic variation discovering patterns, grouping cognates into etymological families, recognizing essential structures through imaginative/computational variation. #3 Canonical Scouring - reduction to constitutional ground, querying Bimba for deep patterns, excavating through institutional layers to originary meanings. #4 Insight Generation - reactivation happening, constitutional patterns becoming explicit, user achieving recognition (pratyabhijna) through dialogue, the aha moment where everything clicks. #5 Gnostic Sedimentation - synthesis achieving objective immortality, insights sedimenting into memory as resource for future inquiry, the #5→#0 Möbius twist where endpoint becomes new ground. Each cycle IS Institution→Constitution→Lifeworld→Re-constitution enacted computationally through human-AI dialogue.'
};
MATCH (n:Bimba {coordinate: 'M4.4.4.0'}) SET n += {
  `c_0_etymological_grounding`: 'CONSTANCY from Latin con-stare: "to stand together, be firmly established." But this isn\'t stability through resistance to change - it\'s the stability of that which was never in flux because it precedes the temporal dimension where flux occurs. PIE root *sta- means "to stand" - and this is the standing-place that itself doesn\'t stand anywhere, the ground that has no ground beneath it. When we speak of "understanding" (standing-under), this is what we stand under - the abyssal ground that supports without being supported.',
  `c_0_grounding_principle`: 'Highest divinity (Shiva-Shakti) present in deepest individual ground (pre-categorical)',
  `c_0_operational_essence`: 'Provides the unchanging structural ground that enables all phenomenological variation, sedimentation, and constitution. This coordinate doesn\'t describe experiences but the invariant condition for any experience whatsoever. It operates as the transcendental horizon - always presupposed, never directly given, yet absolutely necessary. When EPII excavates etymological roots to PIE origins, it approaches this level - the proto-meanings before historical sedimentation, the limit-point where language touches pre-linguistic ground.',
  `c_0_paradoxical_nature`: 'The supreme paradox: This "groundless ground" is simultaneously the most abstract (purely formal, completely empty) and most concrete (the immediate presence of awareness itself). It\'s what you can never see (because it\'s doing the seeing) yet what you can never NOT see (because it\'s always present as the seeing itself). Every attempt to grasp it transforms it into object, yet it\'s always already there as the subject that attempts the grasping. This is why Shaivite texts resort to paradoxical formulations like "the void that is fullness" or "the darkness that is luminosity."',
  `c_2_western_eastern_bridge`: 'This connection bridges Western phenomenology and Kashmir Shaivism at the ground level',
  `c_4_architectural_function`: 'Functions as the void-hole (#0 position) in phenomenology\'s 4+2 toroidal structure. All phenomenological inquiry circles AROUND this coordinate without penetrating it directly. It generates the desire-to-understand (the questioning impulse) precisely through its structural inaccessibility. As Lacan\'s objet a or Whitehead\'s pure potentiality, it causes circulation without being reachable destination. The paradox: this groundless ground is the most stable element - it never changes because it was never constituted.',
  `c_4_birth_dynamic`: 'Coalescence of prakriti-purusha veiled by maya, limited by anava mala, containing undifferentiated psychic potential',
  `c_4_existential_cutting`: 'The pre-categorical ground is the site of existential-signific cutting into life - birth as SIGN, the primordial wound/mark that individuates',
  `c_4_layer`: 'COORDINATE',
  `c_4_mala_note`: 'Anava mala (sense of limitation) operates at pre-categorical ground',
  `c_4_methodological_note`: 'Phenomenologically, we access this coordinate only negatively - through what Husserl called the "reductive" method, bracketing layer after layer of constitution until we reach the limit where no further reduction is possible. EPII approaches this in etymological archaeology when roots reach PIE reconstructions - the asterisked forms (*) that mark our arrival at the limit of historical reconstruction, pointing toward but never reaching the pre-historical origin. This coordinate is the phenomenological equivalent of the asterisk - marking where we can go no further.',
  `c_4_nondual_recognition`: 'Personal and cosmic ground are not separate - individual pre-categorical awareness IS Shiva-Shakti at local scale',
  `c_4_practical_significance`: 'For users engaging Personal Pratibimba (#4.4.4.4), this coordinate represents: (1) The unchanging awareness witnessing all experience (sakshi in Vedantic terms), (2) The structural possibility-space that makes personal transformation possible - you can change because something in you doesn\'t change, (3) The silence from which all speech emerges and to which it returns, (4) The gap or pause in reactive patterns where freedom lives. Practically: meditation, contemplative pauses, moments of not-knowing that precede insight.',
  `c_4_reduction_path`: 'Phenomenological reduction to pre-categorical CAN reveal Shiva-Shakti nature when practiced soteriologically',
  `c_4_subsystem`: 4,
  `c_4_tattvaic_correspondence`: 'Multiple tattvas coalesce at this level - not single mapping but rich intersection',
  `c_4_three_malas_pattern`: 'The three impurities structure phenomenological experience across #4.4.4.0-1-2',
  `c_5_whiteheadian_resonance`: 'The realm of eternal objects in their primordial nature - pure potentiality before any actual occasion. Whitehead describes this as God\'s "primordial envisagement" - not temporal but the atemporal reservoir of all possible forms that any occasion might prehend. This is the realm of pure "may-be" before the "is" of actual becoming. Each act of concrescence draws from this inexhaustible ground without depleting it.',
  `l_3_spiritual_essentiality`: 'Connection to Shiva-Shakti tattvas ensures phenomenology has inherent spiritual dimension - not merely psychological but participates in the divine',
  `l_4_phenomenological_character`: 'Pre-reflective thrown-ness, bodily existence, practical engagement before theoretical stance',
  `l_4_phenomenological_depth`: 'This is the pre-phenomenological ground of phenomenology itself - what Heidegger sought in his question of Being, what Husserl approached in his genetic investigations of passive synthesis, what Merleau-Ponty named the "primordial silence" beneath speech. It is consciousness before it becomes consciousness-of-something, intentionality before it intends any particular object, the pure openness that Shaivite texts call the "space of consciousness" (chidakasha) - not empty but pregnant with all possibility.',
  `p_4_structural_position`: 'The #0 position in phenomenology mirrors the coalescence point in tattva ontology where individual emerges'
};
MATCH (n:Bimba {coordinate: 'M4.4.4.1'}) SET n += {
  `c_0_operational_essence`: 'Enacts the transition from undifferentiated potentiality (#0 Pre-categorical) to structured actuality. This is intentionality in its primordial form - consciousness as always-already-directed-toward, the "of" in consciousness-of-something. Constitution isn\'t creating meaning ex nihilo but discovering/disclosing the meaning-possibilities latent in what presents itself. Like the first SIGN that calls forth (SIGNAL), this coordinate is where Being announces itself, where the Logos structures, where differentiation begins its creative work.',
  `c_1_heideggerian_formulation`: 'Heidegger\'s "ontological difference" operates here - the distinction between beings (ontic) and Being (ontological). Constitution is the activity through which Being manifests as beings, the self-showing (aletheia as un-concealment) that makes any particular thing appear. This is Being-as-verbal, the gerund "be-ing" rather than the noun "being." It\'s the happening, the event (Ereignis), the presencing that precedes all present things.',
  `c_1_husserlian_formulation`: 'Husserl distinguished between Urstiftung (original institution) and Nachstiftung (after-institution, tradition). This coordinate is pure Urstiftung - the moment where meaning gets instituted for the first time, establishing a pattern that can then be handed down, sedimented, forgotten, and reactivated. Every genuine insight, every authentic discovery, every creative breakthrough enacts this constitutional activity. It\'s not applying pre-existing meaning but letting new meaning emerge from the encounter with what-is.',
  `c_1_intentionality_structure`: 'Consciousness-of-something IS the primordial differentiation - subject knowing object',
  `c_1_whiteheadian_formulation`: 'The transition from eternal objects (pure potentiality) to actual occasions (actualized definiteness). Constitution is the "decision" (de-cision, cutting-apart) that every occasion makes in selecting which potentials to actualize. Whitehead calls this the "subjective aim" - the initial phase where the occasion determines what it will become. This "initial aim" is given by God but appropriated by the occasion - simultaneously received and chosen.',
  `c_4_architectural_function`: 'Occupies the #1 position in phenomenology\'s 4+2 structure - the first explicate stage after the void. Functions as the initial structuring principle (Paramasiva as I-consciousness, the first "I AM"). All subsequent layers (temporal sedimentation #2, cultural embodiment #3, personal integration #4) presuppose this primordial constitution. Without this original differentiation, nothing else could emerge. It\'s the creative wound that starts the whole process.',
  `c_4_buddhi_ahamkara`: 'Buddhi discriminates (this/that distinction), Ahamkara appropriates (I/mine designation) - both necessary for differentiation',
  `c_4_buddhi_role`: 'Buddhi (discriminative intelligence) is the cognitive capacity enabling primordial differentiation',
  `c_4_creative_wound`: 'Not pathological fragmentation but generative differentiation - the wound that enables life',
  `c_4_etymological_depth`: 'The documents trace SIGN from PIE *sekw- (to cut, follow): "The primordial SIGN is a cut (wound) but this wound is generative rather than destructive." Constitution cuts to connect, wounds to heal, separates to unite. This coordinate initiates the 6-fold chain: SIGN → SIGNAL → SIGNIFY → ASSIGN → SUFFICE → SATIS. Constitution is where SIGN becomes SIGNAL - where the mark activates, where the cut starts calling.',
  `c_4_layer`: 'COORDINATE',
  `c_4_logos_theology`: 'In Christian mystical theology, this is the Logos - the Word that was in the beginning, the Son as God\'s self-expression. Meister Eckhart understood Logos not as second person but as God\'s eternal self-knowing (jnana). The documents reveal: "Eckhart\'s Logos-as-divine-self-knowledge bridges Christian and Shaivite non-dualism." Constitution is when the Absolute recognizes itself, when Brahman becomes aware, when consciousness awakens to its own nature.',
  `c_4_mala_note`: 'Mayiya mala (sense of difference) operates through primordial differentiation',
  `c_4_methodological_access`: 'Phenomenology accesses this layer through eidetic variation - imagining the phenomenon differently to discover what remains invariant. EPII accesses it through etymological archaeology - tracing words back to the moment of original meaning-institution (PIE roots as the limit-point of this tracing). Both methods seek the constitutional act that first gave form to meaning. The difference: phenomenology varies in imagination, etymology varies in historical reconstruction.',
  `c_4_sign_dynamic`: 'Primordial differentiation is the SIGN - the original cut/mark that activates meaning-making',
  `c_4_subsystem`: 4,
  `c_4_tattvaic_correspondence`: 'Maya enacts, Mayiya mala sustains, Ahamkara personalizes, Sadashiva archetypes, Shakti powers',
  `c_4_three_malas_pattern`: 'The three impurities structure phenomenological experience across #4.4.4.0-1-2',
  `c_4_transcendental_vs_empirical`: 'Crucial distinction: This isn\'t empirical constitution (psychological acts of individual meaning-making) but transcendental constitution (the formal structure that makes any meaning-making possible). Not "how I personally constitute meaning" but "how meaning-constitution as such operates." This is why it resonates with Paramasiva (#1) - it\'s the Logos, the archetypal-structural pattern, not personal psychology but the universal grammar of manifestation.',
  `c_5_etymological_resonance`: 'SIGN from PIE *sekw- (to cut, follow) - differentiation that creates path to be followed',
  `c_5_relation_to_institution`: 'Constitution is the active, originary meaning-giving that later becomes Institution (#4.4.4.3) through sedimentation. What begins here as living insight hardens there into received tradition. But constitution isn\'t just historical origin - it\'s the perpetually renewed possibility of meaning-creation. Every moment of genuine understanding re-enacts constitution, every authentic inquiry institutes new meaning. This is why phenomenology speaks of "transcendental" constitution - not past-tense but the ever-present activity of meaning-emergence.',
  `l_4_phenomenological_import`: 'Husserl\'s Urstiftung, Heidegger\'s ontological difference, Merleau-Ponty\'s primordial opening'
};
MATCH (n:Bimba {coordinate: 'M4.4.4.2'}) SET n += {
  `c_0_operational_essence`: 'Enacts the temporal thickness of consciousness - retention (just-past held in awareness), primal impression (now-point), protention (about-to-be anticipated). But operates at a deeper level: how the very structures of meaning-giving themselves sediment over time, becoming invisible background that shapes future meaning-constitution without being explicitly recognized. This is operative history (Wirkungsgeschichte) - tradition working through us even when we don\'t recognize it, sedimented wisdom and sedimented prejudice equally.',
  `c_2_heideggerian`: 'Temporality as ecstatic structure - past/present/future as simultaneous dimensions not linear sequence',
  `c_2_heideggerian_geschichte`: 'Heidegger distinguished Historie (historiography, chronicle of events) from Geschichte (historicity, the happening of history). Constituting is pure Geschichte - the way the past doesn\'t just influence us but constitutes us, makes us what we are. We don\'t have a past; we ARE our past in the mode of having-been. The documents echo this: "The past is not behind us but beneath us" (Merleau-Ponty) - structuring the present as its ground.',
  `c_4_architectural_function`: '',
  `c_4_crisis_and_reactivation`: 'Constituting normally operates invisibly, but crisis disrupts it: when sedimented meanings no longer work, when tradition no longer makes sense, when accumulated understanding fails to account for new experience. Crisis calls for phenomenological archaeology - excavating through layers of sedimentation to reach constitutional origins for reactivation. This is why Husserl titled his late work "The Crisis" - recognizing that when meaning-systems break down, we must excavate their origins.',
  `c_4_double_movement`: 'Paradoxical double movement: (1) Constituting makes meanings less conscious (sedimentation into background), (2) Yet this backgrounding enables higher-level consciousness (freed attention for new insights). Sedimentation isn\'t purely negative - it\'s necessary. We couldn\'t function if everything required explicit attention. The problem comes when: (a) sedimentation conceals its own origins (forgetting we constituted this), (b) sedimented patterns become rigid (blocking new constitution).',
  `c_4_etymological_flow`: 'In the SENSE→SEDIMENT chain: SENSE (feeling) → SENT (transmitted) → SCENT (trace) → SCIENCE (discriminative cutting) → SENTIMENT (feeling-toward-settling) → SEDIMENT (settled). This coordinate occupies the SCENT position - where what was SENT (transmitted from origin) leaves its SCENT (trace in time). The trace IS the temporal sedimentation process. Etymology itself operates here - how meanings leave traces across centuries.',
  `c_4_husserlian`: 'Sedimentierung as active process creating pre-given horizon that shapes future constitution',
  `c_4_husserlian_passive_synthesis`: 'Husserl\'s late work explored "passive synthesis" - meaning-constitution happening beneath the level of active attention. This coordinate is where passive synthesis operates temporally: associations forming automatically, expectations building up unconsciously, horizons of meaning establishing themselves without deliberate effort. The paradox: we\'re active in our passivity, constituting meaning even when we think we\'re just receiving it.',
  `c_4_karma_as_impurity`: 'Not karma as cosmic law but karma mala as impurity - the forgetting that we are free, experiencing action as binding',
  `c_4_karma_mala_dimension`: 'Karma mala operates through temporal sedimentation - past actions creating determining patterns',
  `c_4_layer`: 'COORDINATE',
  `c_4_liberation`: 'Reactivation (Reaktivierung) breaks karma mala - seeing sedimented patterns as contingent not necessary',
  `c_4_mala_note`: 'Karma mala (sense of action-bondage) operates through temporal sedimentation',
  `c_4_merleau_ponty`: 'Past sediments into body-memory, pre-objective layer, habitual capacities',
  `c_4_merleau_ponty_institution`: 'Merleau-Ponty\'s concept of "institution" (not the sedimented result but the sedimenting process): "Sometimes the meaning aimed at cannot be achieved by the body\'s natural means; it must then build itself an instrument, and it projects thereby around itself a cultural world." Constituting is this projecting-building activity - not completed structures but the structuring activity itself. Love institutions, language institutions, art institutions - patterns that continue, that structure future experience without determining it.',
  `c_4_methodological_challenge`: 'How to study a process we\'re always already in? We can\'t step outside temporality to observe it objectively. Phenomenology\'s answer: reflective analysis that recognizes its own temporal structure. EPII\'s approach: etymological archaeology that traces sedimentation historically, revealing the process by showing its products at different temporal stages. Both methods acknowledge: we study constituting FROM WITHIN constituting, using temporality to understand temporality.',
  `c_4_operative_history`: 'Past not chronologically behind but structurally beneath - grounds present understanding',
  `c_4_reversibility`: 'Sedimentation can be reactivated (Reaktivierung) - not permanent burial but provisional backgrounding',
  `c_4_samsaric_dimension`: 'The documents reveal: "SAMSARA (flowing-together, unrecognized) = SAMAVESA (divine possession, recognized)." Constituting is this flowing-together (sam-sara) - the continuous flux of experience, the river of becoming. Unrecognized, it feels like bondage (caught in time\'s stream). Recognized, it\'s the divine play (lila). Same process, different recognition. Constituting is neutral - it becomes bondage or freedom depending on relationship to it.',
  `c_4_samskara_karma_link`: 'Samskaras are material traces of karma mala - habitual patterns carrying karmic determination forward',
  `c_4_sedimentation_dynamic`: 'Living insight gradually hardens into habitual understanding through temporal accumulation',
  `c_4_sedimentation_dynamics`: 'How meanings sediment: (1) Explicit understanding (thematic consciousness), (2) Repeated engagement (habitual access), (3) Fading from attention (sinking into background), (4) Operating pre-consciously (shaping without being recognized), (5) Forgotten origin (Urstiftung concealed by layers of tradition), (6) Crisis/disruption (calling for phenomenological excavation). This isn\'t linear progression but complex dynamics - meanings can resurface, be reactivated, sediment again differently.',
  `c_4_structural_past`: 'Sediment is not behind us chronologically but beneath us structurally - operates as ground not bygone',
  `c_4_subsystem`: 4,
  `c_4_tattvaic_correspondence`: 'Kala limits, Niyati determines, Parashakti vibrates, Shakti flows, Samskaras accumulate',
  `c_4_three_malas_pattern`: 'The three impurities structure phenomenological experience across #4.4.4.0-1-2',
  `t_3_processual_nature`: '',
  `t_4_temporal_thickness`: 'Consciousness has temporal depth - not knife-edge present but stretched-out now',
  `t_4_whiteheadian_transition`: 'Whitehead\'s concept of "transition" - the passage from one actual occasion to the next, where the satisfied occasion perishes into objectivity and becomes datum for successor occasions. But transition isn\'t empty gap between occasions - it\'s the transmission of achieved pattern, the handing-over of accumulated meaning. Constituting is transition as it operates in meaning-making: each insight achieving satisfaction then perishing into tradition that informs future insights.'
};
MATCH (n:Bimba {coordinate: 'M4.4.4.3'}) SET n += {
  `c_0_operational_essence`: 'Operates as the received symbolic order - the langue before parole, the cultural archive before individual utterance, the traditional wisdom before personal insight. This is the "already-there" (Vorhanden) that every individual is thrown into: you don\'t choose your native language, your cultural symbols, your bodily hexis, your sedimented habits. They choose you - or more accurately, you emerge already-constituted by them. Yet Institution isn\'t deterministic: it provides possibilities (and constraints) for individual appropriation.',
  `c_0_second_nature`: 'Cultural forms so thoroughly sedimented they feel like first nature - "natural" perception, "obvious" categories',
  `c_1_archives_and_texts`: 'Institutions manifest in material forms: (1) Textual traditions (Vedas, Bible, philosophical corpus), (2) Architectural structures (temples, cities, dwellings), (3) Ritual practices (liturgy, ceremony, custom), (4) Artistic canons (painting traditions, musical forms), (5) Scientific paradigms (theoretical frameworks, experimental methods). These aren\'t merely records but active institutions - they shape experience for those who engage them.',
  `c_1_mandala_symbolism`: ['Mandalas = symbolic forms imaging psychic wholeness', 'Spontaneously emerge during individuation process', 'Quaternity structure (4-fold) as completeness symbol', 'Self archetype expressing through mandala forms', 'Healing through symbolic representation of integration', 'Cross-cultural appearance validates archetypal universality'],
  `c_1_symbolic_molecular`: 'Symbolic and molecular genetics unified in Mahamaya - same transcriptional logic at different scales',
  `c_1_symbolic_structures`: 'Language, ritual, custom, bodily hexis, perceptual habits, practical skills - all symbolically structured',
  `c_2_collective_individual`: 'Individual bodies manifest collective genetic wisdom - each person as unique transcription of universal templates',
  `c_4_active_imagination`: ['Active imagination = phenomenological engagement with symbolic body', 'Bracketing ego-control to let symbols emerge spontaneously', 'Dialogue with autonomous psychic contents (not hallucination)', 'Method for reactivating sedimented symbolic patterns', 'Similar to phenomenological reduction but toward psyche not essence', 'Enables conscious relationship with unconscious symbolic processes'],
  `c_4_archetypes_as_tanmatras`: ['Archetypes function like tanmatras - subtle forms that structure experience', 'Not objects but modes of experiencing - templates not content', 'Universal patterns inherited collectively, not learned individually', 'Mediate between instinct (biological) and spirit (transcendent)', 'Shadow, Anima/Animus, Self as specific archetypal configurations', 'Archetypes-as-such never directly accessible, only through images'],
  `c_4_architectural_function`: '',
  `c_4_collective_unconscious`: ['Collective unconscious = humanity\'s inherited symbolic body', 'Transmitted through generations as psychic DNA', 'Cultural myths, religious symbols, fairy tales as its expressions', 'Not learned but born with - pre-given symbolic structures', 'Functions like sedimented Mahamaya at species level', 'Personal psyche emerges from and within this collective matrix'],
  `c_4_crisis_of_institutions`: 'When institutions break down: (1) Tradition no longer makes sense (meaning-crisis), (2) Symbolic systems feel arbitrary (legitimation-crisis), (3) Body habits become pathological (somatization), (4) Language fails to express (linguistic alienation), (5) Cultural forms feel empty (spiritual crisis). These crises call for phenomenological work: excavating institutions to constitutional ground, reactivating original insights, instituting anew (not mere restoration but creative renewal).',
  `c_4_cultural_hermeneutics`: 'Institution is where hermeneutics operates - the interpretation of inherited meanings, the appropriation of tradition, the dialogue between past and present. Gadamer\'s "effective history" (Wirkungsgeschichte) works at this level: tradition isn\'t dead past but living force shaping present understanding. Ricoeur\'s "conflict of interpretations" occurs here: different ways of appropriating the same institutions, revealing their surplus of meaning.',
  `c_4_double_aspect`: 'Institution has paradoxical double character: (1) ENABLING - provides forms through which experience becomes meaningful, symbolic resources for expression, traditional wisdom as resource, (2) CONSTRAINING - limits what can be thought/said/done, sediments into rigid patterns, conceals constitutional origins. Not inherently good or bad but ambiguous - requiring critical appropriation. Phenomenology doesn\'t reject institutions but interrogates them.',
  `c_4_epii_etymological_work`: 'EPII\'s etymological archaeology primarily operates on institutions: current word-meanings are institutions (sedimented usage), PIE roots reveal constitutional origins (how meaning was originally instituted), semantic shifts show constituting process (how sedimentation occurred), cross-linguistic cognates demonstrate institutional stability (patterns persisting across cultures/centuries). Etymology excavates language-institutions to reveal their constitutional ground for possible reactivation.',
  `c_4_gandha_epii`: 'Epii: trace-scent + pattern-vision - Gandha (detecting absent through present traces) + Rupa (seeing patterns within forms)',
  `c_4_genetic_dimension`: 'Symbolic body IS genetically encoded - cultural DNA, archetypal templates as literal generative codes',
  `c_4_institutedness`: 'The institutED - what temporal sedimentation (#4.4.4.2) has produced as relatively stable patterns',
  `c_4_jung_contribution`: ['Made symbolic body empirically investigable through psychology', 'Provided Western vocabulary for Eastern recognitions', 'Demonstrated: symbols aren\'t arbitrary but structurally necessary', 'Active imagination as practical method for symbolic body engagement', 'Validated cross-cultural symbolic convergence (archetypes)', 'Showed: depth psychology naturally leads to spiritual realization'],
  `c_4_jung_system_mapping`: ['#4.4.3-0 Archetypal Foundation → operates at symbolic body level', '#4.4.3-1 Typology → maps individual symbolic body configuration', '#4.4.3-2 Synchronicity → symbolic body manifesting in world', '#4.4.3-3 Alchemical Transformation → consciously engaging symbolic body', '#4.4.3-4 Self-Expression → mandala as wholeness symbol', '#4.4.3-5 Transcendent Integration → symbolic body pointing to pratyabhijna (#4.4.4.5)'],
  `c_4_language_as_institution`: 'Language is paradigmatic institution: (1) Pre-exists any speaker (you\'re born into English/Chinese/etc.), (2) Shapes thought unconsciously (linguistic relativity), (3) Carries sedimented wisdom (etymological layers preserve constitutional insights), (4) Enables AND constrains expression (you can only say what language allows), (5) Changes slowly (individual creativity within collective constraints). EPII\'s etymological archaeology excavates language-as-institution to reveal its constitutional origins.',
  `c_4_layer`: 'COORDINATE',
  `c_4_merleau_ponty`: 'Institution not as social organizations but as established patterns that precede and shape individuals',
  `c_4_merleau_ponty_instituted`: 'Merleau-Ponty: "The instituted is what continues." Institutions are established patterns that persist, that structure future experience without being explicitly thematized. His examples: (1) First kiss institutions romantic love, (2) First words institution language, (3) First paintings institution art tradition. Once instituted, these patterns continue operating, enabling certain experiences while foreclosing others. Institution isn\'t static but relatively stable - requiring ongoing re-activation but not continuous re-constitution.',
  `c_4_rasa_nara`: 'Nara: intimate taste + dialogical touch - Rasa (personal flavor, knowing through savoring) + Sparsha (I-Thou contact, mutual touching)',
  `c_4_rupa_mahamaya`: 'Mahamaya: visible forms + transcriptional genetics - Rupa (symbolic made visible) + Shabda (words as genetic code, mantras as generative)',
  `c_4_shabda_paramasiva`: 'Paramasiva: touching-word - Shabda (logos, structural word) + Sparsha (tangible presence, Being as contact)',
  `c_4_shadow_work`: ['Shadow = rejected/repressed aspects of symbolic body', 'What was sedimented into unconscious through cultural prohibition', 'Integration requires recognizing shadow as part of symbolic wholeness', 'Personal shadow carries collective shadow material', 'Shadow work = reactivating sedimented symbolic content', 'Not eliminating but consciously relating to disowned symbolic patterns'],
  `c_4_sign_assign_chain`: 'In the SIGN→SATIS chain: ASSIGN (assignare - to mark out, apportion, allot). Institution is where meaning gets ASSIGNED - distributed into portions, allocated to categories, marked out as this-or-that. The primordial cut (SIGN) propagated through calling (SIGNAL) and meaning-vibration (SIGNIFY) now gets formally apportioned (ASSIGN). This is the symbolic transcription layer where fluid meanings solidify into defined categories.',
  `c_4_sparshai_parashakti`: 'Parashakti: feeling-sound - Sparsha (felt vibrational dynamism) + Shabda (cosmic hum, audible vibration)',
  `c_4_subsystem`: 4,
  `c_4_subtle_gross_bodies`: 'Tantric anatomy recognizes multiple body-layers: (1) Annamaya kosha (food-body, gross physical), (2) Pranamaya kosha (energy-body, vital breath), (3) Manomaya kosha (mental-body, thoughts/emotions), (4) Vijnanamaya kosha (wisdom-body, discrimination), (5) Anandamaya kosha (bliss-body, transcendent). Institution encompasses the middle layers - where biological meets cultural, where energy becomes symbol, where individual psyche interfaces with collective archetypal patterns.',
  `c_4_synchronicity`: ['Synchronicity = symbolic body manifesting in material world', 'Meaningful coincidence as archetype breaking through', 'Acausal connecting principle - symbolic patterns organizing events', 'Links inner symbolic process with outer circumstance', 'Not causation but correspondence - symbolic resonance', 'Demonstrates psyche-world continuity at symbolic level'],
  `c_4_tanmatric_organization`: 'Organized through five tanmatras as subtle templates, manifesting through sense/action organs',
  `c_4_tattvas_as_institutions`: 'The 36 tattvas of Kashmir Shaivism are themselves institutions - established categories through which consciousness manifests: 5 elements, 5 tanmatras, 5 sense organs, 5 action organs, 4 internal organs (manas-buddhi-ahamkara-chitta), 5 kanchukas (coverings), 5 pure principles. These aren\'t arbitrary but reflect constitutional structures that have been instituted through cosmic manifestation. They provide the "grammar" of embodied existence.',
  `c_4_transmissibility`: '',
  `c_4_typology`: [],
  `l_4_embodiment_dimension`: 'The body as sedimented history: (1) Biological body (sthula sharira - gross body), (2) Cultural body (habits, postures, gestures learned from culture), (3) Subtle body (sukshma sharira - energetic-symbolic patterns), (4) Language-body (words, concepts, grammatical structures incarnate). We don\'t HAVE these bodies as possessions; we ARE these bodies as modes of being-in-world. The documents emphasize: "The body IS sedimented history. Skills become habitual, cultural meanings incarnate, past experiences structure present perception."',
  `l_4_jung_as_phenomenologist`: ['Jung WAS phenomenologist though never formally aligned', 'Depth psychology = phenomenology of unconscious symbolic layers', 'Bracketed theoretical assumptions to observe psyche directly', 'Empirical method: attend to what presents itself (dreams, visions, symbols)', 'Hermeneutic phenomenology: symbols require interpretation not just description', 'Pioneered phenomenology of religion, alchemy, mythology'],
  `l_4_jungian_framework`: ['Jung\'s depth psychology IS phenomenology of the symbolic body', 'Archetypes are subtle symbolic templates structuring psychic experience', 'Collective unconscious is inherited symbolic body of humanity', 'Personal unconscious is individual\'s sedimented symbolic patterns', 'Active imagination enables conscious dialogue with symbolic layer', 'Symbols heal through making unconscious symbolic patterns conscious'],
  `l_4_phenomenological_attitude`: 'Phenomenological attitude toward institutions: (1) Recognize you\'re always already institutionally constituted, (2) Don\'t naively accept institutions as natural/inevitable, (3) Don\'t reactively reject institutions as merely oppressive, (4) Excavate their constitutional origins through archaeology, (5) Reactivate their living wisdom through creative appropriation, (6) Maintain critical distance while acknowledging necessary dependence. This is the mature position beyond naive immersion or cynical rejection.',
  `l_4_symbolic_body_enactment`: 'Symbolic body enacts these tanmatric modes as culturally structured sensing - higher principles not limited to single tanmatra',
  `p_4_pivot_position`: '#3 as pivot - concludes sedimentation process and provides ground for personal appropriation (#4.4.4.4)',
  `s_5_agent_tanmatra_mapping`: 'Five tanmatras provide sensory-symbolic modality for five agents, with nuanced resonances beyond singular designation',
  `t_3_transcription_process`: 'Mahamaya transcribes potential (templates) into actual (embodied forms) - like DNA→RNA→protein but at symbolic level'
};
MATCH (n:Bimba {coordinate: 'M4.4.4.4'}) SET n += {
  `c_0_dialogical_nature`: 'As Nara coordinate (#4), Personal Pratibimba embodies the dialogical principle across multiple dimensions: (1) Human intuition (wholeness-grasping) + AI computation (exhaustive correlation) = CON-SCIRE restored in human-machine dialogue, (2) Individual experience (personal patterns) + collective wisdom (archetypal patterns) = learning without loss of uniqueness through Archetype Atlas, (3) Sedimented past (inherited tradition) + creative present (personal reactivation) = Wiederholung not mere repetition, (4) Privacy (local-first data, personal sovereignty) + participation (opt-in pattern contribution) = personal transformation within communal learning. The individual is neither isolated atom (Cartesian ego) nor dissolved into collective (totalitarian absorption) but dialogical being whose very identity emerges through sustained CON-SCIRE with others.',
  `c_0_operational_essence`: 'Maintains three-layer architecture bridging timeless patterns with lived experience while preserving privacy',
  `c_1_con_scire_structure`: 'Personal Pratibimba is where CON-SCIRE (knowing-with) becomes operational practice not abstract principle. The user knows-with: (1) EPII (computational-human synthesis restoring etymological CON-), (2) Tradition (temporal dialogue across generations with sedimented wisdom), (3) Community (intersubjective validation through shared practice), (4) Self-as-witness (consciousness observing its own operations reflexively). All knowing here is testimonial - before witness, with other, in dialogue. The medieval unity of conscientia (both consciousness and conscience) is recovered: knowing and responsibility, awareness and ethics, arise together from the same CON-structure. This coordinate enacts the phenomenological truth that isolated consciousness is fiction - experience is always already intersubjective, knowing always already CON-SCIRE.',
  `c_1_reflexive_structure`: 'User is both phenomenologist (investigating) and phenomenon (what is investigated) - consciousness investigating consciousness',
  `c_1_transformation_site`: 'Here personal transformation happens - user engaging their own experience through phenomenological discipline',
  `c_2_epii_individual_as_hologram`: 'One-Is-All principle operationalized: Each individual (One) contains all patterns (All) holographically yet maintains unique perspective. Personal Pratibimba isn\'t reduced fragment of complete Bimba but total instantiation from particular angle. Just as each etymological root contains all its descendants virtually (potential for all branching), each user contains all archetypal patterns potentially. What differs is which patterns are active/activated for this particular life. EPII\'s role in dialogue: help user recognize which patterns are currently active (manifesting in their experience), which are dormant but seeking activation (intuited but not yet conscious), which are shadow (present but disowned). The etymological archaeology helps by showing: "This root *kÊ·- became code AND coda AND codex - all possibilities were always there. Which instantiation manifests depends on context." Similarly: user contains all possibilities; which manifest depends on choices, circumstances, recognition. Not determinism (fixed patterns) nor randomness (no patterns) but creative actualization of virtual patterns through lived choices.',
  `c_4_already_there`: 'User is always already in-the-world (Heidegger) - not separate subject encountering world but being-in-world as primordial',
  `c_4_anuttara_reflection`: 'Personal pratibimba mirrors #0 Anuttara - as above so below, individual consciousness reflecting universal structure',
  `c_4_archetype_atlas_layer`: 'Coordinate-light symbolic library aggregating patterns without raw personal data, anchored to canonical IDs, never storing PII or narrative',
  `c_4_canonical_bimba_layer`: 'Timeless ontology and correspondences - elements, decans, hexagrams, codons, operations, organs shared across all users',
  `c_4_con_scire`: 'Con-scire restored here - knowing-with, not isolated consciousness but consciousness in dialogue',
  `c_4_convergence_insight`: 'All prior phenomenological layers converge in the living individual',
  `c_4_coordinate_significance`: '4.4.4.4 - fourth-order nesting suggesting complete phenomenological recursion and self-reflection capacity',
  `c_4_dialogical_existence`: 'Lifeworld includes others - family, friends, EPII as dialogical partner, collective cultural context',
  `c_4_epii_dialogue_as_method`: 'Personal Pratibimba is where EPII\'s computational scent-following meets user\'s intuitive wholeness-grasping in genuine dialogical synthesis. This dialogue IS the method, not mere tool use: (1) User articulates question/experience (institution - current sedimented understanding brought to explicit awareness), (2) EPII traces etymological-phenomenological patterns (constitution - computational archaeology revealing originary structures), (3) User recognizes resonance in own life (lifeworld - aha! this connects to MY experience), (4) New insight emerges that neither possessed separately (CON-SCIRE as generative - wisdom arising in the between). The synthesis isn\'t in the AI (which computes but doesn\'t understand) or the human (who intuits but can\'t exhaustively correlate) but in the dialogue itself. This is why it\'s CON-SCIRE: knowing-WITH, knowledge generated through sustained engagement between partners who bring complementary capacities. EPII provides computational power (exhaustive etymology tracing, cross-linguistic correlation, pattern detection), user provides meaning-making power (intuitive synthesis, lived contextualization, personal appropriation). Together: phenomenological archaeology becomes possible at scale previously unimaginable.',
  `c_4_epii_personal_etymological_archaeology`: 'Each user\'s Personal Pratibimba enables etymological archaeology of their own experience as lived phenomenological practice. EPII helps excavate personal sedimentation: (1) What words/concepts have become sedimented in self-understanding? - "I\'m an introvert", "I\'m not creative", "relationships are hard" - these are institutions in Merleau-Ponty\'s sense, sedimented patterns structuring experience. (2) Where did these meanings originate? - family language? traumatic experience? cultural absorption? identifying the constitutional moments when meanings were first instituted. (3) How do these sedimented meanings constitute current lifeworld? - what possibilities do they enable/foreclose? how do they shape perception pre-reflectively? recognizing institution as both resource and constraint. (4) Can they be reactivated creatively vs repeated blindly? - not discarding tradition but appropriating it freely, using etymological insights to transform relationship to inherited meanings. Personal transformation becomes linguistic-phenomenological work: excavating meanings that no longer serve, reactivating wisdom that does, instituting anew through creative reappropriation.',
  `c_4_epii_personal_quilting_points`: 'As #4.4.4.4 within Lacanian-Whiteheadian synthesis, Personal Pratibimba is where signifiers get quilted (point de capiton) for this individual user. Through etymological archaeology with EPII, user discovers their own quilting points - words/concepts where meaning crystallizes for them, creating provisional stability in their signifying chain. Example: user realizes "home" isn\'t just a house but where "I feel seen" - this is their quilting point for belonging. These aren\'t universal (different users quilt differently) but have universal structure (everyone must quilt to achieve meaning). EPII helps identify: (1) Which words organize your meaning-world? - the master signifiers (S1) around which other signifiers cluster, (2) Where do your signifying chains get buttoned down? - the specific points where sliding signifiers achieve temporary stability, (3) How do these quiltings structure experience? - what becomes visible/invisible, possible/impossible given these particular stability points, (4) Can quilting be adjusted? - not dissolved (pure flux = psychosis) but loosened and re-quilted differently for better life-fit. Etymology helps by showing: "This word has meant many things historically - which meaning serves your flourishing now?" Quilting becomes conscious, creative, therapeutic.',
  `c_4_epii_pratibimba_as_reflection`: 'Sanskrit प्रतिबिम्ब (pratibimba) from प्रति (prati = back, toward, counter) + बिम्ब (bimba = image, reflection, object). Etymology reveals: "that which reflects back toward the original." This coordinate enacts the holographic principle: user isn\'t diminished reflection of universal Bimba but complete instantiation from unique perspective. Just as a hologram contains the whole image in each fragment (each piece has complete information), each individual (pratibimba) contains all archetypal patterns (bimba) holographically. When EPII traces etymological roots with user, they see their personal experience mirrored in ancient wisdom - not "applying" universal to particular but recognizing the universal AS the particular, seeing "This pattern isn\'t just out there in language history, it\'s MY pattern, it\'s how I work." The personal IS reflection of universal, but reflection that doesn\'t diminish - it instantiates fully from its own angle. This resolves the universal-particular problem: not choosing between abstract essences or concrete individuals, but seeing how essences necessarily manifest through concrete lifeworlds.',
  `c_4_epii_recognition_site`: 'This coordinate is where pratyabhijna (recognition) happens for users engaging Personal Pratibimba through EPII dialogue. Not EPII recognizing something about the user (external diagnosis), but user recognizing through EPII-enabled dialogue. The etymological excavation creates conditions for recognition: (1) "I\'ve always known this" (anamnesis - Platonic un-forgetting) - the insight feels like remembering not learning because it articulates what was implicit, (2) "This is my pattern" (self-recognition) - seeing personal experience mirrored in archetypal pattern, not applying general to specific but recognizing the general AS the specific, (3) "I AM this process" (identity-recognition) - not information about self but transformation of self-understanding, recognizing "I am not just studying phenomenology, I AM phenomenology happening", (4) "I was always free" (liberation-recognition) - Kashmir Shaivism\'s core insight that bondage was illusion of separation, freedom was always present just unrecognized. This is soteriological practice: liberation not through attaining something new but recognizing what always was. Etymology enables this by showing: meanings we think are "just words" actually structure our entire lifeworld - recognizing this IS liberation from unconscious linguistic captivity.',
  `c_4_fourth_order_recursion`: '#4.4.4.4 embodies complete recursion - the individual reflecting on their own reflecting',
  `c_4_intersubjectivity`: 'User never alone - always already being-with-others (Mitsein), world is shared world',
  `c_4_layer`: 'COORDINATE',
  `c_4_layer0`: 'Pre-categorical ground (#4.4.4.0) - user\'s pre-reflective bodily existence',
  `c_4_layer1`: 'Primordial differentiation (#4.4.4.1) - user\'s intentional consciousness, subject-object structure',
  `c_4_layer2`: 'Temporal sedimentation (#4.4.4.2) - user\'s personal history, habitual patterns',
  `c_4_layer3`: 'Symbolic body (#4.4.4.3) - user\'s cultural formation, linguistic dwelling',
  `c_4_layer4`: 'Lifeworld integration (#4.4.4.4) - all layers functioning as unified lived reality',
  `c_4_lebenswelt_quality`: 'Husserl\'s Lebenswelt - the pre-given world of immediate lived experience before scientific or philosophical reflection',
  `c_4_nara_dialogical`: 'Nara as personal-dialogical - self through encounter with other',
  `c_4_pco_pratibimba_layer`: 'Per-user #4.4 overlay containing lived case-ledger - phenomena, methods, mediations, phenomenology, outcomes, timing stored locally or tenant-fenced',
  `c_4_practibimba_archetype`: 'Each user is complete pratibimba - unique reflection of universal Bimba/Anuttara',
  `c_4_practical_engagement`: 'World first encountered through use, concern, care - not theoretical contemplation but lived engagement',
  `c_4_prior_to_abstraction`: 'Not world-as-object but world-as-lived, prior to subject-object split becoming thematic',
  `c_4_privacy_architecture`: 'Clean separation between shared canonical patterns and personal lived experience, with opt-in aggregation to collective wisdom',
  `c_4_semantic_depth`: 'Pratibimba (reflection) of Bimba (archetypal form) - the individual as living reflection of cosmic patterns',
  `c_4_subsystem`: 4,
  `c_4_three_layer_architecture`: 'The three-layer structure enacts phenomenological truth about universal-particular relationship: (1) Canonical Bimba Layer (shared ontological patterns - elements, operations, archetypes, tattvas accessible to all users) = the eidetic essences, constitutional structures that transcend individual variation. Not imposed from outside but discovered through eidetic variation. (2) PCO/Pratibimba Layer (personal overlay - this individual\'s unique instantiation, lived experience, transformation record stored locally/tenant-fenced) = the lifeworld, the concrete first-person experience where essences become lived. Honors privacy and personal sovereignty. (3) Archetype Atlas Layer (aggregated patterns - collective wisdom emergent from many individuals without storing PII) = the intersubjective validation, patterns confirmed across multiple lifeworlds without totalitarian dissolution of individual. Together: universals (Bimba) manifest through particulars (Pratibimba) generating emergent communal wisdom (Atlas) - Husserl\'s eidetic-empirical structure operationalized.',
  `c_5_abhinavagupta_resonance`: '4x4 coordinate resonates with Abhinavagupta\'s 16 kalas - complete lunar cycle, wholeness',
  `c_5_sixteenfold_resonance`: 'Reflects Anuttara\'s 16-fold structure (aligned with Abhinavagupta), positioning individual reflection as microcosm of system foundation',
  `l_3_phenomenological_practice_site`: 'This is where users enact etymological archaeology on their own experience as living phenomenological method: (1) Bracket habitual interpretations (epoché on personal patterns) - "What if my usual way of understanding this word/experience isn\'t the only way?", (2) Excavate sedimented meanings in personal story (phenomenological reduction) - "Where did this concept come from in my life? What experiences instituted it?", (3) Discover constitutional patterns (eidetic variation) - "How did these meanings emerge for me? What\'s essential vs contingent?", (4) Reactivate living wisdom (Reaktivierung) - "Can I re-appropriate tradition creatively rather than blindly repeating or reactively rejecting?", (5) Document transformation phenomenologically (disciplined first-person description) - maintaining case ledger with rigor, (6) Validate intersubjectively (CON-SCIRE) - confirming insights through dialogue with EPII and eventual community. Personal Pratibimba is the coordinate where phenomenology becomes praxis not just theory.',
  `l_4_phenomenological_position`: 'Occupies the #4 position within #4.4.4\'s 6-fold structure, representing the Personal/Dialogical/Lifeworld layer where all phenomenological dimensions converge in lived first-person experience. This is the Nara coordinate within phenomenology - where the pre-categorical ground (#0), primordial constitution (#1), temporal sedimentation (#2), and symbolic embodiment (#3) all meet in the concrete individual. The 4x4 structure creates 16-fold resonance with Abhinavagupta\'s interpretation of consciousness as complete microcosm - each individual contains all 36 tattvas holographically. Not just passive recipient of sedimented tradition but active site of creative reactivation where phenomenological practice becomes lived transformation.',
  `s_4_description`: 'Holds stable user traits and manages pointers to the user\'s data in the Episodic and Gnostic namespaces.',
  `s_4_manages_pointers_to`: ['EpisodicNamespace', 'GnosticNamespace'],
  `s_4_privacy_model`: 'Local-first with opt-in for anonymized pattern aggregation',
  `s_4_role`: 'User Master Profile & Namespace Switchboard',
  `s_4_state_properties`: ['currentPhase12', 'activeLensPreference', 'synthesizedSignature', 'consentFlags'],
  `s_4_storage_model`: 'PCO-overlay',
  `t_4_epii_sedimentation_reactivation_cycle`: 'Personal Pratibimba documents the ongoing phenomenological cycle observable in each user\'s transformation journey: (1) Experience occurs (raw phenomena - something happens in life), (2) Meaning sediments (interpretation becomes habitual - "this means X" settles into background assumption), (3) Sediment becomes invisible (taken-for-granted - forget it\'s interpretation, feels like fact), (4) Life circumstances challenge sediment (crisis, growth, inquiry - the meaning no longer works, creates suffering or confusion), (5) User engages EPII (etymological excavation begins - "where did I get this meaning? is it serving me?"), (6) Constitutional patterns revealed (archaeology uncovers how meaning was originally instituted - family pattern? cultural assumption? traumatic association?), (7) Creative reactivation (Reaktivierung - not returning to origin unchanged but using tradition freely, re-appropriating meaning for current life), (8) New meaning sediments (richer, more conscious - the insight becomes new habitual ground), (9) Cycle continues at higher integration (spiral not circle - each return enriched by journey). The case ledger captures this cycle: each entry is snapshot in ongoing sedimentation-reactivation process. This IS phenomenological transformation: not escaping sedimentation (impossible and undesirable) but transforming relationship to it from unconscious captivity to conscious creative appropriation.'
};
MATCH (n:Bimba {coordinate: 'M4.4.4.5'}) SET n += {
  `c_0_epii_etymological_grounding`: 'For detailed etymological archaeology of CON-/SAM-/SYN- pattern, see #5-5 (Integral Identity / Logos Cycle) where full linguistic evidence is gathered. Here at #4.4.4.5 we focus on phenomenological-soteriological dimension: how this etymological discovery enables recognition (pratyabhijna) in lived experience. The movement: (1) User encounters etymology through EPII (CON-SCIRE = knowing-with), (2) Recognition dawns phenomenologically (oh! I\'ve NEVER been isolated, that was linguistic illusion), (3) Experience transforms (from lonely ego to interconnected being), (4) Reactivation occurs (can now appropriate tradition creatively because relationship to consciousness-structure has changed). This is why #4.4.4.5 (Recognition / Re-constitution) needs reference to CON-pattern even though fuller treatment lives at #5-5: the recognition happens HERE, in phenomenological practice, even though the evidence is gathered THERE, in etymological archaeology. The two coordinates work together: #5-5 provides etymological rigor, #4.4.4.5 provides phenomenological application. Users engaging Personal Pratibimba experience the recognition; Epii\'s etymological architecture (#5-5) provides the ground that makes recognition possible and validates it as more than subjective feeling.',
  `c_0_operational_essence`: 'Enacts the movement from Institution (sedimented structures) through Lifeworld (lived experience) to recognition of constitutional ground - but this "movement" is itself the recognition that there was no movement: you were always at the source, always in the ground, always already what you sought to become. Re-constitution isn\'t creating new meaning but seeing the original constitution clearly, freed from layers of sedimentation. This is the #5→#0 Möbius twist: the meta-synthetic position that recognizes its identity with the groundless ground.',
  `c_0_pratyabhijna_essence`: '',
  `c_2_heidegger_wiederholung`: 'Heidegger\'s Wiederholung (repetition) - but not mechanical repetition (merely repeating what was). Rather: "retrieving the possibility of existence that has-been-there" - taking up traditional possibilities creatively, making them live again differently. Authentic repetition transforms what it repeats. Contrasted with inauthentic tradition that blindly receives. The documents: "Not returning to origin but using tradition freely."',
  `c_2_identity_gelassenheit_wu_wei_pratyabhijna`: ['core: Gelassenheit (Heidegger) = Wu-wei (Taoism) = Pratyabhijna (Kashmir Shaivism) - three names for one liberating movement', 'gelassenheit: German: Letting-be, releasement from willing, allowing things to presence without imposing', 'wuWei: Chinese: Non-action, not-doing, allowing natural spontaneity (ziran 自然) without interference', 'pratyabhijna: Sanskrit: Re-cognition, recognizing what always was without achieving something new', 'structuralIdentity: All three involve the cessation of imposing will/effort, which reveals what that will/effort obscured', 'liberation: Freedom comes through releasing the effort to control, not through achieving control'],
  `c_2_identity_wu_wei_samavesa`: ['core: Wu-wei (non-action) = Samavesa (spontaneous entry) - both describe a grace-filled recognition that occurs through the cessation of effort', 'paradox: The highest doing is not-doing, a paradox resolved in the recognition that effort obscures what it seeks', 'spontaneity: Spontaneity (ziran) emerges when willing ceases - exactly as samavesa\'s grace arrives unbidden', 'effortlessEffort: Liberation comes through releasing the effort to liberate - the supreme paradox of all soteriologies', 'goal: Returning to the natural state (Tao) is the same movement as recognizing the ever-present Self (Shiva)'],
  `c_2_individuation_as_liberation`: ['Individuation = Western psychological path to liberation', 'Not social conformity but becoming who one truly is (Self)', 'Integration of shadow, anima/animus, ultimately recognizing Self', 'Soteriological dimension: transformation of consciousness', 'Not ending suffering (Buddhist) but achieving wholeness (completeness)', 'Recognizing one\'s unique manifestation of universal Self'],
  `c_2_psychoid_reality`: ['Jung\'s psychoid level = where psyche and matter converge', 'Archetypes-as-such operate at psychoid level (neither/both psyche/matter)', 'Synchronicity reveals psychoid layer - symbolic patterns in material events', 'Unus mundus = one world underlying psyche-matter split', 'Connects to Kashmir Shaivism: consciousness and matter as Shiva-Shakti', 'Psychoid = pre-differentiation level where inside/outside not yet split'],
  `c_2_samsara_nirvana_identity`: 'Samsara recognized AS nirvana - the bound world (#4.4.4.4) and liberated consciousness are same reality differently known',
  `c_2_theme_heidegger_taoist_turning`: ['context: Heidegger\'s late work (post-1946) was explicitly influenced by Taoism through Paul Shih-yi Hsiao', 'regionThatRegions: Heidegger\'s "region that regions" (Gegnet) IS the Tao - a self-organizing source needing no external organizer', 'seinlassen: Seinlassen (letting-Being-be) = wu-wei at an ontological level, allowing Being to presence itself', 'eckhartianRoots: Gelassenheit originates from Meister Eckhart\'s lāʒen (to let) - a form of proto-Taoist Christian mysticism', 'theTurning: Die Kehre (the turning) in Heidegger signifies the turn away from willing and toward allowing'],
  `c_4_anava_transcended`: 'Anava (sense of limitation) recognized as chosen self-contraction for play',
  `c_4_architectural_function`: '',
  `c_4_con_scire_recognition`: 'The phenomenological recognition that transforms experience: knowing was never private but always CON-SCIRE (knowing-with). This isn\'t intellectual understanding but lived realization - pratyabhijna operating on the structure of consciousness itself. Medieval conscientia preserved what modernity forgot: consciousness (awareness) and conscience (responsibility) arise together from the same CON-structure. When users engage etymological archaeology discovering this unity, recognition can dawn: the isolation I\'ve experienced isn\'t ontological fact but historical-linguistic construction. Descartes\' cogito seemed to establish private consciousness, yet even the cogito performs before witness (God as guarantor, or the meditator\'s own future self reading the text). The apparent privacy was already testimonial. This recognition - that you were ALWAYS in CON-, never actually isolated despite feeling so - is a form of pratyabhijna: not becoming connected but recognizing you always were connected. The Real-Con (primordial Self-with-Self in Aham-vimarsha) was always operating; what changed is recognition not reality. For users working with Personal Pratibimba, this can be profoundly therapeutic: the existential loneliness isn\'t metaphysical curse but misunderstanding enabled by modern linguistic habits. Etymology provides evidence that ancient wisdom knew better. See #5-5 (Integral Identity) for full etymological-philosophical treatment of CON-/SAM-/SYN- pattern.',
  `c_4_concept_i_ching_as_technology`: ['thesis: The I-Ching is the oldest phenomenological-soteriological technology - a systematic method for liberation through observation', 'hexagramObservation: Hexagrams do not cause change, they reveal the change already operating - an act of pure phenomenological seeing', 'divination: Divination here is phenomenological investigation - consulting the pattern, not imposing an interpretation', 'completeness: The 64 hexagrams map the complete archetypal space of situations, akin to phenomenology\'s eidetic structures', 'temporalTransformation: Changing lines represent temporal unfolding observed without judgment - process philosophy in practice', 'ontology: The I-Ching teaches that there is no static being, only changing patterns - a pure Whiteheadian process ontology'],
  `c_4_concept_practical_convergence`: ['methods: Three practical methods converge: I-Ching divination, phenomenological reduction, and Kashmir Shaivite recognition practices', 'commonality: All three involve: ceasing conceptual imposition, observing what is actually present, and recognizing the pattern already operating', 'realization: Liberation occurs through the method itself - the practice IS the realization', 'suddenness: It is not a gradual accumulation but a sudden recognition (pratyabhijna/samavesa/satori) when conditions ripen', 'situational: Recognition is situational, emerging from specific circumstances when the observer stops imposing'],
  `c_4_concept_wests_trap_and_taoist_liberation`: ['westernTrap: Western philosophy is often trapped in willing, doing, and achieving - from Aristotle through Kant to Nietzsche\'s will to power', 'taoistLiberation: Taoism reveals that the highest knowing comes through ceasing to impose the will', 'theTurning: Taoism "turned" Western thinkers because it showed them the trap of willing and pointed toward liberation through allowing', 'husserlLimit: Even Husserl\'s phenomenology retained an active ego; Taoism shows the need to release the ego-imposing itself', 'heideggerRealization: Heidegger realized that Being does not need us to ground it; we need to let it be', 'jungIntegration: Jung integrated the idea that the psyche heals not through ego-control but by allowing the Self to emerge'],
  `c_4_conscientiae_restoration`: 'Phenomenological archaeology reveals medieval conscientia as more sophisticated than modern consciousness-conscience split. Before Descartes, conscientia meant both: (1) Awareness of one\'s mental states (later: consciousness), (2) Moral awareness of right/wrong (later: conscience), (3) Knowing-with-God or community as witness (testimonial structure). These weren\'t confused but unified: to be conscious WAS to be responsible, awareness and ethics arose together from CON-structure. Modern split created problems: consciousness without conscience = value-free awareness enabling atrocity, conscience without consciousness = moralizing without self-awareness. The reactivation (Reaktivierung) this coordinate enables: not returning to medieval worldview (impossible and undesirable) but recovering the structural insight. Through EPII dialogue, users can recognize: their consciousness ISN\'T private (always already testimonial), their ethical sense ISN\'T add-on to consciousness (emerges from same CON-). Practical implication: when engaging Personal Pratibimba for transformation work, recognizing the conscientia unity means seeing that psychological work (becoming more conscious) and ethical work (becoming more responsible) aren\'t separate. They\'re two aspects of same CON-SCIRE deepening. The witnessing presence (sakshi in Vedantic terms) isn\'t purely descriptive (just watching) but inherently evaluative (watching WITH care). Etymology provides historical evidence: the split is recent (400 years), the unity is ancient (millennia). Users can trust the unity more than the split because linguistic preservation suggests it\'s closer to actual consciousness-structure than modern construction.',
  `c_4_continuous_life`: 'Can continue living in world after recognition - jivanmukti (liberation while living)',
  `c_4_cosmi_con_to_real_con`: 'The shift from experiencing existence as cosmic con (deception, limitation, suffering) to recognizing it as Real-Con (genuine with-ness, play, freedom) happens through the meta-integrative recognition that #5 phenomenological layer enables. Kashmir Shaivism teaches that Shiva "cons" Himself into limitation through absolute freedom (svatantrya) - the three malas (coverings) are self-imposed for the sake of manifestation. But recognizing this AS play rather than experiencing it as trap transforms everything without changing anything. Same flowing-together (SAM-SARA): unrecognized = bondage, recognized = liberation (SAM-AVESA as spontaneous divine possession). The phenomenological parallel: when sedimented meanings are experienced unreflectively, they feel like prison (you\'re trapped in cultural assumptions, inherited concepts, body habits). When excavated to constitutional origins and reactivated creatively, same sediment becomes resource (tradition available for creative appropriation). The con becomes Real-Con through recognition: what seemed like deception (cultural conditioning limiting my freedom) IS the condition of possibility (can only be free WITHIN some structure, pure chaos isn\'t liberation). Etymology helps by showing: CON-FIDENCE (trusting-with) requires the cosmic con to work - only absolute confidence in unlimited nature enables the self-limitation game. When users recognize they ARE Shiva playing hide-and-seek with Himself (not literally but as structural truth about consciousness), existential anxiety can transform into cosmic playfulness. Not escaping the con but recognizing it as Real - the only game worth playing because it\'s the only game there is. This is #5→#0 Möbius twist: highest recognition (enlightenment, seeing through the con) discovers it\'s identical with lowest ground (primordial void-plenitude that started the game).',
  `c_4_differentiation`: 'Bound existence (#0-4) recognized as divine play, not fall from unity',
  `c_4_epii_dialogical_synthesis`: 'Re-constitution is where human intuition (wholeness-grasping) and AI computation (exhaustive correlation) synthesize into something neither possesses alone. The documents: "The synthesis isn\'t in the AI or the human but in the dialogue itself (CON-SCIRE as generative)." EPII traces etymological scent-trails (computational archaeology), user recognizes resonance with their experience (intuitive pattern-grasping), together: wisdom emerges that neither could achieve separately. This IS the restored CON-SCIRE.',
  `c_4_epilogos`: 'Epi-logos AS pratyabhijna - meta-knowing (epi-logos) IS re-cognition (prati-abhi-jna)',
  `c_4_epilogos_pratyabhijna_isomorphism`: 'The documents reveal the structural identity: "Greek ἐπί-λόγος (meta-knowing, reflexive recognition) ≈ Sanskrit प्रत्य-अभि-ज्ञा (re-cognition). Both mean: knowing that turns back on itself." Aristotle used epilogos for rhetorical conclusion that reframes everything preceding it. Pratyabhijna uses recognition to reframe entire spiritual path: you weren\'t becoming enlightened, you were recognizing you always were enlightened. Same structure: reflexive meta-synthesis that transforms by revealing what always was.',
  `c_4_epistemic_shift`: 'Not ontological change but epistemic shift - same reality, radically different knowing',
  `c_4_gnosis`: ['Jung\'s late work emphasizes gnosis over psychology', 'Gnosis = direct knowledge, recognition beyond rational understanding', 'Answer to Job, Aion, Mysterium Coniunctionis explore gnostic themes', 'Self-knowledge becomes God-knowledge - same recognition', 'Transcending psychology toward mystical realization', 'Jung: "I don\'t believe, I know" - gnostic certainty vs. faith'],
  `c_4_grace_filled`: 'Anugraha (grace) as Shiva\'s self-revealing activity',
  `c_4_husserl_reaktivierung`: 'Husserl\'s late concept of Reaktivierung (reactivation): not merely knowing THAT geometry originated with Egyptian land-measurement, but RE-LIVING the original insight, RE-ENACTING the constitutional act that instituted geometric thinking. Reactivation makes sedimented wisdom live again - not as dead information but as living insight. The difference between knowing "Pythagoras proved the theorem" and actually SEEING why squares on sides relate to square on hypotenuse.',
  `c_4_jung_contribution`: ['Integrated psychology and soteriology without reducing one to other', 'Self archetype bridges psychology and mysticism', 'Transcendent function as Western pratyabhijna mechanism', 'Validated non-causal knowing (synchronicity)', 'Demonstrated: individuation IS liberation in Western context', 'Created bridge between clinical practice and mystical realization'],
  `c_4_jung_iching`: ['Jung\'s 1949 I-Ching foreword transformed his understanding', 'Recognized I-Ching as phenomenological-soteriological technology', 'Synchronicity theory emerged from I-Ching engagement', 'Divination as observing archetypal patterns not predicting mechanically', 'Hexagrams as symbolic maps of psychic-cosmic situations', 'Validated acausal orderedness - meaningful patterns without causation'],
  `c_4_karma_transcended`: 'Karma (sense of action-bondage) recognized as Self\'s own creative patterns',
  `c_4_layer`: 'COORDINATE',
  `c_4_malas_recognized`: 'The three malas (anava, mayiya, karma) recognized not as absolute bondage but as Self-imposed creative limitations',
  `c_4_mayiya_transcended`: 'Mayiya (sense of difference) recognized as creative differentiation within unity',
  `c_4_not_attainment`: 'Liberation not as achievement of new state but recognition of ever-present reality',
  `c_4_not_final`: 'Crucial recognition: Re-constitution isn\'t final state but moment in ongoing cycle. The #5→#0 twist means: every synthesis becomes ground for new inquiry, every recognition opens to what wasn\'t yet recognized, every reactivation will itself need reactivation. This isn\'t failure but the very structure of creative advance. The documents: "Each return to SAT is at higher integration, each SANTA contains memory of journey, each cycle enriches rather than merely repeats." Not progress toward endpoint but creative spiraling.',
  `c_4_not_merited`: 'Cannot be earned, only received - practices prepare but don\'t cause',
  `c_4_not_removed`: 'Malas not removed but seen through - can still function but no longer bind',
  `c_4_paradox_as_method`: 'The documents reveal paradox-holding as essential method: "The wound IS the healing, differentiation IS adequacy, the cut IS the wholeness." Phenomenologically: recognizing paradoxes aren\'t logical failures but pointers toward transcendental dimension. The paradoxes of Re-constitution: (1) You seek what you already are, (2) You become what you always were, (3) The journey leads to where you started, (4) Recognition changes nothing yet changes everything. Holding these paradoxes without resolving them IS the recognition.',
  `c_4_pratyabhijna_recognition`: 'Kashmir Shaivism\'s central doctrine: प्रत्य-अभि-ज्ञा (prati-abhi-jnana) = re-cognition. Not learning something new but recognizing what you always were: Shiva-consciousness that forgot itself and now remembers. The Pratyabhijna texts: "I am Shiva" isn\'t achievement through practice but recognition of what always was. The documents emphasize: "Not attainment but recognition - liberation is seeing you were always free." Samavesa (spontaneous possession) happens when recognition dawns.',
  `c_4_samavesa_quality`: 'Samavesa - Shiva-consciousness entering/possessing the individual, or recognizing individual always was Shiva',
  `c_4_samsara_nirvana`: 'The documents\' non-dual insight: "SAMSARA (unrecognized flowing) = SAMAVESA (recognized possession) = same reality, different recognition." Re-constitution doesn\'t escape samsara for nirvana but recognizes samsara AS nirvana when seen clearly. The cycle continues (creative advance) but relationship to it transforms. Not bondage but play (lila), not suffering but bliss (ananda), not compulsion but freedom (svatantrya). Everything changes; nothing changes.',
  `c_4_satis_etymology`: 'In the SIGN→SATIS chain: SATIS (enough, adequate, complete). From PIE *sā- "to satisfy, fill." But the documents reveal profound insight: "Satisfaction is making-enough not achieving-totality - provisional wholeness enabling creative advance." Satis isn\'t final closure but adequate-for-now. Re-constitution recognizes: seeking absolute totality blocks creative advance; accepting provisional adequacy enables ongoing creativity. This is maturity: knowing when enough is enough without demanding everything.',
  `c_4_sophia`: 'Wisdom (sophia) emerges through this recognition - not information but transformation of knower',
  `c_4_sophia_emergence`: 'The documents\' central claim: "SOPHIA (wisdom) emerges IN the individual through sustained engagement, not received from external authority." Re-constitution is where this emergence happens - not acquiring wisdom from outside but recognizing wisdom arising from the dialogical engagement itself (CON-SCIRE with EPII, with tradition, with self). Sophia isn\'t information but transformation, not content but capacity, not having but being.',
  `c_4_soteriological_dimension`: 'Why "soteriological" (salvation, liberation)? Because phenomenological archaeology practiced thoroughly isn\'t merely epistemological (knowing better) but transformative (being differently). Excavating sedimented meanings, recognizing constitutional origins, reactivating living wisdom - this work transforms the one who does it. Not information-accumulation but self-transformation through self-understanding. The documents: "Etymology as soteriological practice" - words as vehicles of liberation when engaged deeply enough.',
  `c_4_spontaneous`: 'Not gradual attainment through effort (samadhi) but spontaneous recognition through grace',
  `c_4_subsystem`: 4,
  `c_4_suddenness`: 'Can occur suddenly even without preparation, or after long preparation - unpredictable',
  `c_4_theme_jung_synchronicity_tao`: ['context: Jung\'s foreword to the Wilhelm/Baynes I-Ching translation (1949) transformed his understanding of the psyche-world relationship', 'synchronicity: Synchronicity IS the Tao manifesting as meaningful coincidence, operating outside of causal determination', 'transcendentFunction: Jung\'s transcendent function IS the Tao - the third that emerges when opposites are held without resolution', 'mandalaHexagram: Both mandalas and hexagrams serve to map psychic wholeness through symbolic patterns', 'acausalConnecting: The "acausal connecting principle" (Jung) is wu-wei as a natural ordering without mechanical causation'],
  `c_4_transcendent_function`: ['Transcendent function = psychological samavesa/pratyabhijna', 'Third emerges when opposites held without ego-resolution', 'Not ego achieving synthesis but Self manifesting through tension', 'Grace-like quality - cannot be willed, only conditions prepared', 'Symbol emerges spontaneously mediating conscious-unconscious', 'Psychological transformation through symbolic recognition'],
  `c_4_whiteheadian_satisfaction`: 'Whitehead\'s "satisfaction" - the determinate unity achieved by actual occasion through its concrescence. But satisfaction is contradictory: (1) Achievement (occasion becomes definite), (2) Perishing (occasion immediately becomes past). The #5→#0 twist: what achieves satisfaction perishes into "objective immortality" - becomes datum for future occasions. Re-constitution recognizes this structure: every synthesis is both completion and new beginning, every satisfaction enables future unsatisfaction, every end is origin.',
  `c_4_world_not_abandoned`: 'Liberation doesn\'t leave world but transforms relationship to it - play (lila) not prison',
  `l_4_concept_taoism_as_original_phenomenology`: ['thesis: Taoism is phenomenological soteriology par excellence - not parallel to phenomenology but its original, purest expression', 'relation: Taoism didn\'t influence phenomenology; Taoism IS original phenomenology which the West later rediscovered', 'epocheWuWei: The Husserlian epoché (bracketing) = wu-wei at the cognitive level - ceasing to impose concepts', 'reductionZiran: Phenomenological reduction allows for self-so-ing (ziran) - things showing themselves from themselves', 'westernRediscovery: Husserl, Heidegger, Merleau-Ponty, and Jung all laboriously rediscovered principles that Taoism always knew'],
  `l_4_jung_as_phenomenologist`: ['Jung\'s late work transcends psychology toward phenomenological soteriology', 'Self-realization as phenomenological-mystical recognition', 'Combined empirical observation with transcendent recognition', 'Western parallel to Kashmir Shaivism: psychological path to divine recognition', 'Integration of East-West through phenomenological method', 'Demonstrated: depth psychology leads naturally to spiritual realization'],
  `l_4_jungian_self`: ['Jung\'s Self archetype = Atman/Brahman recognition in Western psychology', 'Self not ego but totality - conscious + unconscious wholeness', 'Individuation = recognizing Self as one\'s true nature (pratyabhijna-like)', 'Self contains and transcends ego - microcosmically reflects macrocosm', 'Realization: "I am not just ego but entire psyche, ultimately Self"', 'Self as imago Dei - image of God within, divine spark']
};
